COLLDATA("hifzhadith","en",[[1,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Those who go to excess are ruined.” He said it three times."],[2,"Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Delay the noon prayer until it cools.”"],[3,"Abu Hurayrah reported that a man was supplicating with two fingers, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Make it one, make it one.”"],[4,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh said: A man passed through the mosque carrying arrows, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Hold onto their iron tips.”"],[5,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fasting is a shield.”"],[6,"Muʿadh ibn Jabal reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Fasting is a shield.”"],[7,"ʿA’ishah reported: I sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ to go out in battle, and he said: “Your striving is pilgrimage.”"],[8,"Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The pilgrimage is ‘Arafah.”"],[9,"Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Profit goes with liability.”"],[10,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: “Do not engage in artificial bidding.”"],[11,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Exchange gifts, and you will love one another.”"],[12,"Jābir reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “ʿUmrā is valid.”"],[13,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “ʿUmrā is valid.”"],[14,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A return is like a campaign.”"],[15,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “War is deception.”"],[16,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said: We formed ranks on the day of Badr, but a group of us moved out in front of the rank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at them and said: “With me, with me.”"],[17,"Abu Hurayrah said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me: from what was creation created?” He said: “From water.”"],[18,"ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿūd said: The moon split during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and became two parts. He said to us: “Bear witness, bear witness.”"],[19,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “My dear son.”"],[20,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me from what creation was made.” He replied: “From water.”"],[21,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “My son.”"],[22,"Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān said: “Intercede and you will be rewarded. Sometimes I intend to carry out a matter, but I delay it so that you may intercede and thereby receive a reward, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Intercede and you will be rewarded.’”"],[23,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one whose advice is sought is entrusted.”"],[24,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “My son.”"],[25,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The extremists who go beyond proper bounds are ruined.” He said it three times."],[26,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about intrusive whisperings, and he said: “That is pure faith.”"],[27,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The bell is among the musical instruments of Satan.”"],[28,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “What is the Trumpet?” He replied: “A horn into which it will be blown.”"],[29,"ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Deeds are judged only by their endings.”"],[30,"Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Blessing is with your elders.”"],[31,"Ibn ‘Abbas said: The dawn prayer was commenced, and a man stood to pray the two units. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pulled his garment and said: “Are you praying the dawn prayer as four units?”"],[32,"Ibn ‘Umar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Beat (the coming of) Fajr with Witr.” (i.e., perform Witr before Fajr arrives.)"],[33,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “On buried treasure, one-fifth is due.”"],[34,"Hudhayfah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[35,"Jabir reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[36,"ʿAbdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[37,"Rafiʿ ibn Khadij reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one performing cupping and the one receiving it have broken the fast.”"],[38,"Thawban reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one performing cupping and the one receiving it have broken the fast.”"],[39,"Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be easy with others, and ease will be shown to you.”"],[40,"Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you weigh, then give extra.”"],[41,"Jābir reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “ʿUmrā is an inheritance for its people.”"],[42,"Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: The Prophet ﷺ said, “The sister’s son is one of them.”"],[43,"‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The killer gets nothing.”"],[44,"Ibn ‘Abbas said: If people would reduce the bequest from one-third to one-fourth, that would be better, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One-third, and one-third is much.”"],[45,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best marriage is the easiest one.”"],[46,"Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that retaliation applies in the case of a tooth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Book of Allah prescribes retaliation.”"],[47,"Amr ibn Shuayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ said: “For the wound that exposes the bone, there are five.”"],[48,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The tanning of a dead animal’s hide is its purification.”"],[49,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"],[50,"Jābir reported: The people said, “O Messenger of Allah, the arrows of Thaqīf have pierced us, so supplicate to Allah against them.” He instead prayed: “O Allah, guide Thaqīf.”"],[51,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced me and said: “O Allah, teach him the Book.”"],[52,"Jābir narrated: The people said: “O Messenger of Allah, the arrows of Thaqīf have caused us severe suffering, so supplicate to Allah against them.” He said: “O Allah, guide Thaqīf.”"],[53,"Abū Hurayrah used to say: “Were I to see gazelles grazing in Madinah, I would not frighten them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The area between its two lava plains is sacred.”"],[54,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beautify the Qur’an with your voices.”"],[55,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “What is the Trumpet?” He replied: “It is a horn into which one will blow.”"],[56,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “What is the Trumpet?” He replied: “It is a horn into which one will blow.”"],[57,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[58,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[59,"Ḥudhayfah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[60,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The maternal aunt holds the status of a mother.”"],[61,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is the mirror of the believer.”"],[62,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever remains silent is saved.”"],[63,"Umm Kurz narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Leave the birds in their places.”"],[64,"Ṭāriq ibn Ashyam narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Killing will be sufficient for my Companions.”"],[65,"ʿAmmār narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rebellious group will kill you.”"],[66,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “What is the Trumpet?” He replied: “A horn that will be blown.”"],[67,"Maysarah al-Fajr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a Prophet?” He replied: “While Adam was between the soul and the body.”"],[68,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, when was Prophethood established for you?” He replied: “While Adam was between the soul and the body.”"],[69,"Umm Kurz al-Kaʿbiyyah may Allah be pleased with her reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Prophethood has gone, and the glad tidings remain.”"],[70,"Jundub ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Sufyān al-Bajalī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “I will precede you to the Basin.”"],[71,"Muʿāwiyah al-Qushayrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent.”"],[72,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Contentious disputation concerning the Qurʾān is disbelief.”"],[73,"ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Nothing makes water impure.”"],[74,"Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have repeatedly emphasized the siwāk to you.”"],[75,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number.”"],[76,"Umm Salamah , may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If she sees wetness, then let her perform ghusl.”"],[77,"ʿĀʾishah reported that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[78,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[79,"Zayd ibn Thābit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Wuḍūʾ is required because of what fire has touched.”"],[80,"ʿĀʾishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform wuḍūʾ because of what fire has touched.”"],[81,"Abū Ṭalḥah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Perform wuḍūʾ because of what fire has cooked.”"],[82,"Umm Ḥabībah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever touches his private part must perform wuḍūʾ.”"],[83,"‘A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Delay the noon prayer during heat.”"],[84,"Samurah ibn Jundub reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The middle prayer is the ‘Asr prayer.”"],[85,"Abu Umamah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The imam is responsible, and the caller to prayer is entrusted.”"],[86,"Sa‘d ibn Abi Waqqas said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was supplicating with two fingers, and he said: “Make it one, make it one,” and he pointed with the index finger."],[87,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Saying ‘Subhan Allah’ is for men, and clapping is for women.”"],[88,"Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The best prayer is the one with the longest qunut (standing).”"],[89,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Pray Witr before you reach morning (before Fajr comes in).”"],[90,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build mosques in an exaggerated, lofty manner.”"],[91,"Abū Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The illness/persistent pain of the believer is an expiation for his sins.”"],[92,"Ibn Masʿūd reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The believer dies with sweat upon the forehead.”"],[93,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever washes a deceased person should bathe.”"],[94,"Jarir ibn ʿAbdullah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who commits injustice in collecting charity is like the one who withholds it.”"],[95,"Ibn Abi Mulaykah reported that ʿA’ishah gave something in charity, then ordered Barirah to go and look at it. So the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not count closely, lest it be counted closely against you.”"],[96,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “How excellent are dates as the believer’s pre-dawn meal.”"],[97,"Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: My father wants to take all my wealth. He said: “You and your wealth belong to your father. Indeed, the best of what you eat is from your own earnings, and the wealth of your children is from your earnings, so consume it with ease.”"],[98,"Al-Miqdam ibn Ma‘di Karib narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “Measure your food, and blessing will be given to you.”"],[99,"Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A borrowed item is to be returned, and a manihah (an animal lent for its milk) is to be returned.”"],[100,"Abu Umamah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A borrowed item is to be returned, and a manihah (an animal lent for its milk) is to be returned.”"],[101,"Abu Umamah al-Bahili said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The guarantor is liable, and the debt must be paid.”"],[102,"Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Settlement is permissible among Muslims.”"],[103,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There should be neither harm nor reciprocating harm.”"],[104,"Aishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever deceives us is not from us.”"],[105,"Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet ﷺ, said: “A town-dweller must not sell on behalf of a desert-dweller.”"],[106,"Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Taking a Muslim’s stray animal for oneself leads to the Fire.”"],[107,"Ibn ʿUmar said: “The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ prohibited ruqbā and said: ‘Whoever grants something as a ruqbā, then it belongs to the one to whom it was granted.’”"],[108,"‘A’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wala’ belongs only to the one who emancipates.”"],[109,"Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The son of a people’s sister is one of them.”"],[110,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “If the newborn gives a cry at birth, he is to inherit.”"],[111,"Ibn ‘Umar narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Clientship belongs only to the one who emancipates.”"],[112,"Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"],[113,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"],[114,"Ibn Mas‘ud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"],[115,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no shighar in Islam.”"],[116,"ʿImran ibn Husayn narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no shighar in Islam.”"],[117,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled: “There is no shighar in Islam.”"],[118,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One suckling and two sucklings do not make marriage unlawful.”"],[119,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One quick suckling and two quick sucklings do not make marriage unlawful.”"],[120,"Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The teeth are equal, and the fingers are equal.”"],[121,"Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no cutting of the hand for the snatcher.”"],[122,"Abdullah ibn Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"],[123,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The expiation for a vow is the expiation for an oath.”"],[124,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.”"],[125,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.”"],[126,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no firstborn sacrifice and no Rajab sacrifice.”"],[127,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no slaughter at graves in Islam.”"],[128,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.”"],[129,"ʿA’ishah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The purification of every hide is its tanning.”"],[130,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Blessing is in the forelocks of horses.”"],[131,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blessing of horses is in chestnut-colored ones.”"],[132,"Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas reported: “On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ emptied his quiver out for me and said, ‘Shoot! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.’”"],[133,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib was asked, “Was the Prophet’s ﷺ face like a sword?” He replied, “No, rather it was like the moon.”"],[134,"Anas was asked about the Prophet’s ﷺ white hairs and replied: Allah did not mar his beauty with extensive whiteness."],[135,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I saw the Prophet ﷺ carrying al-Ḥasan upon his shoulder, saying: “O Allah, I love him, so love him.”"],[136,"Umm Salamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAmmār: “The rebellious group will kill you.”"],[137,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Anṣār are my inner garment, while the people are my outer garment.”"],[138,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was supplicating with my finger and said: “One, one.” He pointed with his index finger."],[139,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about al-nushrah, and he replied: “It is among the works of Satan.”"],[140,"Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr al-Muzanī narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ, while I was still a young servant, say: “ʿAjwah dates and the tree are from Paradise.”"],[141,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who dies from an abdominal illness is a martyr, and the one who dies from plague is a martyr.”"],[142,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Most of the hypocrites of my nation will be among its reciters.”"],[143,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Wrongdoing will become layers of darkness on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[144,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom.”"],[145,"Jābir narrated: It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, do the people of Paradise sleep?” He replied: “No. Sleep is the brother of death.”"],[146,"Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The one who severs family ties will not enter Paradise.”"],[147,"Ibn ʿAbbās said concerning the verse: “O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you?” “This was revealed concerning his bondwoman.”"],[148,"Abū Wā’il narrated that Ḥudhayfah was informed that a certain man used to carry tales between people. Ḥudhayfah said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘A tale-bearer will not enter Paradise.’”"],[149,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I have been sent, and the Hour is like these two.”"],[150,"ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is subjected to a detailed reckoning will perish.”"],[151,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: Abū Jahl said: “If I see Muḥammad praying by the Kaʿbah, I will certainly step upon his neck.” When this reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Had he done it, the angels would have seized him.”"],[152,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors. To which of them should I give a gift?” He replied: “To the one whose door is closer to yours.”"],[153,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom.”"],[154,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom.”"],[155,"Anas narrated: “Had I not heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ‘Do not wish for death,’ I would have wished for it.”"],[156,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no superstitious omen, and the best of it is a good sign.” He was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is a good sign?” He replied: “A good word that one of you hears.”"],[157,"Ḥudhayfah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “A tale-bearer will not enter Paradise.”"],[158,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is to be no estrangement after three days.”"],[159,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Most of the hypocrites of my Ummah will be among its reciters.”"],[160,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Worldly status is wealth, while true nobility is piety.”"],[161,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Trim the mustaches closely and leave the beards.”"],[162,"Anas was asked about the gray hair of the Prophet ﷺ. He replied: “Allah did not mar him with extensive whiteness.”"],[163,"Umm Salamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAmmār: “The rebellious group will kill you.”"],[164,"Jābir ibn Samurah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and the Hour have been sent like these two.”"],[165,"Abū Saʿīd narrated that Ibn Ṣayyād asked the Prophet ﷺ about the soil of Paradise. He replied: “It is fine, white earth of pure musk.”"],[166,"Abū Saʿīd narrated that Ibn Ṣayyād asked the Prophet ﷺ about the soil of Paradise. He replied: “Fine white flour, pure musk.”"],[167,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will the people of Paradise sleep?” He replied: “No. Sleep is the brother of death.”"],[168,"ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty brings nothing except good.”"],[169,"Hāniʾ ibn Hāniʾ reported: ʿAmmār may Allah be pleased with him entered upon ʿAlī may Allah be pleased with him, and ʿAlī said: “Welcome to the good and purified one.” I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “ʿAmmār has been filled with faith to the very ends of his bones.”"],[170,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is sinful disobedience, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[171,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer has protective jealousy, and Allah possesses it more intensely.”"],[172,"Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr may Allah be pleased with them reported that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Nothing possesses greater protective jealousy than Allah.”"],[173,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prophets are alive in their graves, praying.”"],[174,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep.”"],[175,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “My intercession is for the people who committed major sins from my Ummah.”"],[176,"Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what about the intercession?” He replied: “The intercession is for those from my Ummah who committed major sins.”"],[177,"ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is subjected to a detailed examination of his deeds in the reckoning will be ruined.”"],[178,"Anas ibn Mālik may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Supplicate, for supplication repels Divine Decree.”"],[179,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported from the Prophet ﷺ: He narrated it with wording similar to the ḥadīth of Abū Muʿāwiyah."],[180,"Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, the one who declares the lawful unlawful is like the one who declares the unlawful lawful.”"],[181,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with them, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, most of the hypocrites of my Ummah are its reciters.”"],[182,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Most of the hypocrites of this Ummah are its reciters.”"],[183,"ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The siwāk is a means of purification for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.”"],[184,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Most of the punishment of the grave is because of urine.”"],[185,"Ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Expel water from the nose thoroughly twice, or three times.”"],[186,"Abū Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The earth has been made for me a means of purification and a place of prayer.”"],[187,"A man from the Ansar reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Get up, O Bilal, and give us rest through the prayer.” His saying, “Give us rest through the prayer,” means: establish the prayer so that we may find rest through it from the weariness and distractions of worldly life; prayer brings rest to the heart and soul through intimate communion with Allah."],[188,"Al-Mughirah ibn Shu‘bah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The coolness of my eye has been placed in the prayer.”"],[189,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What lies between the east and the west is a direction of prayer.”"],[190,"Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays the two cool prayers enters Paradise.”"],[191,"Umm Salamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best mosques for women are the deepest parts of their homes.”"],[192,"Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A dog, a donkey, and a woman cut off the prayer.”"],[193,"Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid reported that Shurayh al-Hadrami was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: “He does not use the Qur’an as a pillow.”"],[194,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is One (Witr) and He loves Witr.”"],[195,"Ibn ‘Umar narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “Make the last of your night prayer Witr.”"],[196,"‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Witr is one rak‘ah at the end of the night.”"],[197,"Ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you comes to Friday (prayer), let him perform ghusl.”"],[198,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever.”"],[199,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The deceased is punished because of his family’s crying over him.”"],[200,"Samurah ibn Jundub reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The deceased is punished because of the wailing done over him.”"],[201,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you perfume the deceased with incense, do it three times.”"],[202,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: A dead person was mentioned negatively in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: “Do not mention your dead except with good.”"],[203,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not insult the dead, lest you hurt the living.”"],[204,"Al-Barā’ ibn ʿĀzib said: When Ibrāhīm passed away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He has a wet nurse in Paradise.”"],[205,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: “Allah knows best what they would have done.”"],[206,"ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Breaking the bone of the dead is like breaking it while he is alive.”"],[207,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prophets are alive in their graves, praying.”"],[208,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine.”"],[209,"ʿA’ishah said: A lizard was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, but he did not eat it. ʿA’ishah said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, should we not feed it to the poor?” He said: “Do not feed them what you yourselves do not eat.”"],[210,"ʿAdi ibn Hatim said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date.”"],[211,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date.”"],[212,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date.”"],[213,"Abu Hurayrah said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which charity is best?” He said: “The effort of the one who has little, and begin with those whom you support.”"],[214,"Ibn Bujayd al-Ansari al-Harithi reported from his grandmother that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Respond to the poor person, even if only with a burnt hoof.”"],[215,"Anas ibn Malik reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal.”"],[216,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal.”"],[217,"ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal.”"],[218,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take the pre-dawn meal, even if only with a sip of water.”"],[219,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who eats and is grateful is like the one who fasts and is patient.”"],[220,"Nubayshah al-Hudhali said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking.”"],[221,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no continuous fasting,” meaning in fasting."],[222,"Muʿawiyah reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the Night of Decree that he said: “The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh.”"],[223,"Jabir ibn Abd Allah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for.”"],[224,"Qatadah said: I asked Anas: How many times did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform Hajj? He said: One Hajj, and he performed four Umrahs."],[225,"Aishah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, should I not enter the House? He said: “Enter the Hijr, for it is part of the House.”"],[226,"Jabir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A lesser pilgrimage in Ramadan equals a pilgrimage.”"],[227,"Wahb ibn Khanbash said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A lesser pilgrimage in Ramadan equals a pilgrimage.”"],[228,"Abdullah ibn Busr al-Mazini said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Measure your food, and it will be blessed for you.”"],[229,"Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The buyer and seller retain the option as long as they have not separated.”"],[230,"Abu Barzah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The buyer and seller retain the option as long as they have not separated.”"],[231,"Umm Hani’ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to her: “Keep sheep, for there is blessing in them.”"],[232,"Al-Sab ibn Jaththamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no protected reserve except for Allah and His Messenger.”"],[233,"Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no protected reserve except for Allah and His Messenger.”"],[234,"Al-Sharid ibn Suwayd al-Thaqafi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The delay of one who has means makes his honor lawful to speak against and makes punishment lawful.”"],[235,"Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill the elder polytheists and spare their young.”"],[236,"Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Swearing may make the goods sell, but it wipes out the blessing.”"],[237,"Ibn ‘Abbas used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fruit is not to be sold until it can be eaten.”"],[238,"Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Delay in payment by a wealthy person is injustice. If you are referred for payment to a solvent person, accept the transfer, and do not conduct two sales in one sale.”"],[239,"Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, injustice will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[240,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The followers of two different religions do not inherit from one another.”"],[241,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A diseased animal should not be brought to one that is healthy.”"],[242,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The previously married woman has three days, and the virgin has seven.”"],[243,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “A man’s messenger to another man is his permission.”"],[244,"Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah reported that Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth a few nights after her husband’s death, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.”"],[245,"Fatimah bint Qays reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning a woman divorced three times: “She has no housing and no maintenance.”"],[246,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The curse of Allah is upon the one who offers a bribe and the one who takes it.”"],[247,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Insulting a Muslim is sinful rebellion, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[248,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Fighting a Muslim is disbelief, and insulting him is sinful rebellion.”"],[249,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Insulting a Muslim is sinful rebellion, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[250,"Usamah ibn Sharik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No soul bears the crime of another.”"],[251,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Once the gaze has entered, there is no permission.”"],[252,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face.”"],[253,"ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn Samurah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not swear by false gods nor by your fathers.”"],[254,"Anas narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whoever slaughtered before the prayer should repeat it…” the hadith."],[255,"Maymunah narrated that a domestic sheep belonging to one of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Why did you not take its hide and benefit from it?”"],[256,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When the hide is tanned, it becomes pure.”"],[257,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any hide that is tanned has become pure.”"],[258,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the spiny-tailed lizard, and he said: “I do not eat it, but I do not forbid it.”"],[259,"ʿA’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “What an excellent condiment vinegar is.”"],[260,"Abu al-Darda’ narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “One who is addicted to wine will not enter Paradise.”"],[261,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a honey-based drink. He said: “Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden.”"],[262,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is forbidden.”"],[263,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is forbidden.”"],[264,"Abu Dharr al-Ghifari said: I asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Which deed is best?” He said: “Faith in Allah and striving in His path.” The hadith continues."],[265,"Jabir said: They said: “O Messenger of Allah, which striving is best?” He said: “That of one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is spilled.”"],[266,"Musʿab ibn Saʿd said: Saʿd thought that he had superiority over those below him, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Are you given victory except through your weak ones?”"],[267,"Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill the elders of the polytheists and spare their young.”"],[268,"The Mother of the Believers ʿA’ishah said: Among the final instructions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was that he said: “Two religions are not to be left in the Arabian Peninsula.”"],[269,"Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula.”"],[270,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The sun and the moon will be wrapped up on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[271,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAbbas narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “I was given victory by the east wind, and ʿAd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[272,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade walking in one sandal, and said: “Indeed, Satan walks in one sandal.”"],[273,"Ibn ʿAbbas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was given victory by the east wind, and ʿAd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[274,"Anas ibn Malik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Musa ibn ʿImran is the chosen one of Allah.”"],[275,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was granted victory by the east wind, while ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[276,"Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was granted victory by the east wind, while ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[277,"Abū Hurayrah reported: The Companions said, “Messenger of Allah, you joke with us.” He replied, “I say nothing except the truth.”"],[278,"Ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was granted victory by the east wind, while ʿĀd was destroyed by the west wind.”"],[279,"Abū Surayḥah Ḥudhayfah ibn Usayd—or, according to another narration, Zayd ibn Arqam—reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"],[280,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"],[281,"Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ approached. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is my maternal uncle. Let each person show me his maternal uncle!”"],[282,"Umm Mubashshir narrated: A servant of Ḥāṭib came and said: “By Allah, Ḥāṭib will not enter Paradise.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You have lied. He witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah.”"],[283,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: When Ibrāhīm died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He has a wet nurse in Paradise.”"],[284,"Umm Mubashshir narrated: A servant of Ḥāṭib said: “By Allah, Ḥāṭib will never enter Paradise.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You have spoken falsely. He participated in the Battle of Badr and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyah.”"],[285,"Hānīʾ ibn Hānīʾ said: ʿAmmār entered upon ʿAlī. ʿAlī said: “Welcome to the pure one who has been made pure.” Then he said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘ʿAmmār has been filled with faith up to his very bones.’”"],[286,"A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “ʿAmmār has been filled with faith up to his very bones.”"],[287,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Zamzam water is for whatever purpose it is drunk.”"],[288,"Rabīʿah ibn ʿĀmir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Persist in saying: ‘O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.’”"],[289,"A man from Banū Kinānah narrated: I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ during the Year of the Conquest and heard him say: “O Allah, do not disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[290,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, just as You have made my physical form beautiful, make my character beautiful.”"],[291,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, just as You have made my physical form beautiful, make my character beautiful.”"],[292,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The evil eye is real.” He also prohibited tattooing."],[293,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The owner of sick camels must not bring them among the camels of a healthy owner.”"],[294,"Abū Qatādah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen the truth.”"],[295,"Samurah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Qur’an was revealed in seven modes.”"],[296,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best among you are those who learn the Qur’an and teach it.”"],[297,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Most of the hypocrites of this nation will be among its reciters.”"],[298,"ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim al-Ṭāʾī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Jews are those who have incurred wrath, and the Christians are those who have gone astray.”"],[299,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about bitʿ, a drink made from honey. He replied: “Every drink that causes intoxication is forbidden.”"],[300,"Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrated: Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth only a few nights after her husband died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Your waiting period has ended, so marry whomever you wish.”"],[301,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every person’s fate and deeds are fastened to his neck.”"],[302,"ʿĀ’ishah said concerning the words: “The one among them who assumed the greatest share of it”: “It was ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl.”"],[303,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was granted victory through the east wind, while ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[304,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first two disputants to present their case on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.”"],[305,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was granted victory through the east wind, and ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[306,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: They said: “O Messenger of Allah, you joke with us.” He replied: “Indeed, I say nothing except the truth.”"],[307,"Rabīʿah ibn ʿĀmir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Persist in saying: ‘O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.’”"],[308,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you comes for the Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.”"],[309,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was granted victory by the east wind, and ʿĀd were destroyed by the west wind.”"],[310,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The sun and the moon will be folded up on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[311,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was only sent to perfect noble character.”"],[312,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of goodness.”"],[313,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.”"],[314,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Once the gaze has entered, seeking permission is of no benefit.”"],[315,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man’s messenger to another man constitutes his permission.”"],[316,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Spread salām and you will be safe, and arrogance and insolence are evil.”"],[317,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who begins with salām is free of the sin of severing ties and estrangement.”"],[318,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no good in one who does not offer hospitality.”"],[319,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you are invited even to a meal of a sheep’s lower leg, then accept the invitation.”"],[320,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has hair should honor and care for it.”"],[321,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah.”"],[322,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmrah narrated from his paternal uncle that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not combine my name and my kunyah.”"],[323,"Umm Sulaym narrated: She was with the wives of the Prophet ﷺ while a camel-driver was driving their mounts. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Anjashah, drive gently with the glass vessels.”"],[324,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you hear a man saying, ‘The people are ruined,’ then he is the most ruined of them.”"],[325,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Throw dust into the mouths of excessive flatterers.”"],[326,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Removing something harmful from the road is charity.”"],[327,"Abū Barzah narrated: I said: “O Prophet of Allah, teach me something from which I may benefit.” He said: “Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims.”"],[328,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not hurt a Muslim by insulting a disbeliever.”"],[329,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, injustice will be layers of darkness on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[330,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is kufr.”"],[331,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is kufr.”"],[332,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is kufr.”"],[333,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not insult the dead, for by doing so you hurt the living.”"],[334,"Jarmūz al-Hujaymī narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He replied: “I advise you not to be one who frequently curses.”"],[335,"Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ narrated: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is tribal partisanship?” He replied: “That you support your people in wrongdoing.”"],[336,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Most of the hypocrites of this Ummah will be among its reciters.”"],[337,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What do you think of Juʿayl?” I replied: “He is a poor man, like others of his kind among the people.” He asked: “And what do you think of so-and-so?” I replied: “He is a leader among the leaders of the people.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Juʿayl is better than an earthful—or thousands, or something similar—of men like so-and-so.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so is like that, why do you treat him as you do?” He replied: “He is the leader of his people, so through him I seek to win their hearts.”"],[338,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The righteousness of the first generation of this Ummah was through asceticism and certainty, while its later generations will be ruined through miserliness and prolonged worldly hopes.”"],[339,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever.”"],[340,"Zayd ibn Thābit narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, this wealth is green and sweet.”"],[341,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever imitates a people is one of them.”"],[342,"Ḥudhayfah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever imitates a people is one of them.”"],[343,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Change the gray hair, but do not bring it near black.”"],[344,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The evil eye is real.” And he prohibited tattooing."],[345,"Maʿqil ibn Yasār narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Worship during times of harj is like emigrating to me.”"],[346,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Receive glad tidings, O ʿAmmār. The rebellious group will kill you.”"],[347,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “In every generation of my Ummah there are those who precede others.”"],[348,"Jābir ibn Samurah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Before the Hour there will be liars.”"],[349,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Dajjāl is one-eyed, and he is the greatest of liars.”"],[350,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The sun and the moon will be folded up on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[351,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “My intercession is for those among my Ummah who committed major sins.”"],[352,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.”"],[353,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The chief fragrant plant of the people of Paradise is henna.”"],[354,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The Throne shook at the death of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh.”"],[355,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Throne shook at the death of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh.”"],[356,"Umm Salamah may Allah be pleased with her reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.”"],[357,"Umm Ḥabībah, Mother of the Believers may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.”"],[358,"Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who eat the pre-dawn meal.”"],[359,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with them, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother’s womb.”"],[360,"Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah creates every maker and what he makes.”"],[361,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm in doing so.”"],[362,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm in doing so.”"],[363,"ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Overlook the slips of people of upright standing, except in matters requiring prescribed legal punishments.”"],[364,"Khabbāb, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When the Children of Israel were ruined, they resorted to storytelling.”"],[365,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Trim the moustaches and let the beards grow; differ from the Magians.”"],[366,"Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not trim his moustache is not from us.”"],[367,"Salamah ibn Qays, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you perform wuḍūʾ, expel the water from your nose; and when you clean yourself with stones, do so an odd number of times.”"],[368,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you dress and when you perform wuḍūʾ, begin with your right sides.”"],[369,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be thorough in purifying between the fingers, or the Fire will thoroughly reach them.”"],[370,"ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydī said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Woe to the heels and the soles of the feet from the Fire.”"],[371,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The earth has been made for me a place of prayer and a means of purification.” Abridged."],[372,"Mu‘awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The callers to prayer will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[373,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The callers to prayer will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[374,"Anas ibn Malik reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the Jews envy you for the greeting of peace and for saying ‘Amin.’”"],[375,"Al-Bara’ reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you prostrate, place your palms and lift your elbows.”"],[376,"Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, part of completing the prayer is straightening the row.”"],[377,"Ibn ‘Abbas reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The black dog and the menstruating woman cut off the prayer.”"],[378,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been forbidden to pray behind people who are talking and those who are sleeping.”"],[379,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The whole earth is a place of prayer except the bathhouse and the graveyard.”"],[380,"Abu Hurayrah reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill the two black creatures during prayer: the snake and the scorpion.”"],[381,"‘Abdullāh ibn Shaqīq said: I said to ‘Ā’ishah: Did the Prophet ﷺ use to pray Ḍuḥā? She said: No—except when he returned from his absence (i.e., from travel)."],[382,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever comes to the mosque for something, then that is his share (i.e., his portion/reward corresponds to that intention).”"],[383,"Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is to bury it.”"],[384,"Abū Umāmah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Spitting in the mosque is an evil deed, and burying it is a good deed.”"],[385,"The Mother of the Believers Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Going out for Jumuʿah is obligatory upon every adult (one who has reached puberty).”"],[386,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and free the captive.”"],[387,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prompt your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah.”"],[388,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Remember often the destroyer of pleasures,” meaning death."],[389,"Abū Qatādah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you takes charge of his brother, let him make his shroud good.”"],[390,"Bahz ibn Hakim narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ said: “For every five grazing camels, charity is due.”"],[391,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no zakat on less than five awsuq.”"],[392,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no zakat on less than five awsuq.”"],[393,"Abu Umamah al-Bahili reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has people whom He frees from the Fire at every breaking of the fast.”"],[394,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who eat the pre-dawn meal.”"],[395,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting without breaking the fast at sunset. They said: O Messenger of Allah, but you do it. He said: “I am not like you; I am fed and given drink.”"],[396,"Kaʿb ibn ʿAsim al-Ashʿari al-Makhzumi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.”"],[397,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.”"],[398,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAbbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.”"],[399,"Jabir ibn Samurah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights.”"],[400,"Bilal, the Prophet’s caller to prayer, said: “It is within the seven among the last ten nights.”"],[401,"ʿA’ishah said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you regard striving in battle as the best deed, so should we not strive in battle? He said: “No, rather the best striving is a righteous pilgrimage.”"],[402,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in his talbiyah: “Here I am, O God of truth, here I am.”"],[403,"‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Abbās reported that the Prophet ﷺ sent forward the weak members of his household and said: “Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises.”"],[404,"Salamah ibn Nubayt narrated from his father — who had performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ — that he said: I saw him delivering a sermon on the Day of Arafah while on his camel."],[405,"Ali ibn Abi Talib said: Then he — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — came to the place of slaughter and said: “This is the place of slaughter, and all of Mina is a place of slaughter.”"],[406,"Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the purest earning, and he said: “A man’s work with his own hand, and every righteous sale.”"],[407,"Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man entered Paradise because of his lenience when selling, buying, and collecting what was owed to him.”"],[408,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two people should not part except upon mutual satisfaction.”"],[409,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The hand is responsible for what it takes until it returns it.”"],[410,"Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever revives dead land, it belongs to him.”"],[411,"Abdullah ibn Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every sin of the martyr is forgiven except debt.”"],[412,"Usamah ibn Zayd reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no usury when it is hand to hand.”"],[413,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not buy fruits until their ripeness appears.”"],[414,"Abd Allah ibn Abbas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is usury in an advance sale involving habal al-habal.”"],[415,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things are not to be withheld: water, pasture, and fire.”"],[416,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should sell over the sale of another.”"],[417,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A Muslim must not outbid his brother in a transaction.”"],[418,"Abdullah ibn Mas‘ud said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The first matter to be judged among the people will be bloodshed.”"],[419,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A concealed stray camel requires compensation for it and another like it.”"],[420,"Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr reported that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: “Be just between your children; be just between your sons.”"],[421,"Buraydah said: Abu Bakr and ‘Umar proposed marriage to Fatimah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “She is young.” Then ‘Ali proposed to her, and he married her to him."],[422,"Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A flogged fornicator marries none but one like himself.”"],[423,"Anas narrated that ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn ʿAwf married a woman for the weight of a date-stone. The Prophet ﷺ saw the signs of marriage happiness on him and asked him, and he said: I have married a woman for the weight of a date-stone."],[424,"ʿA’ishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “There is no divorce and no emancipation in a state of coercion.”"],[425,"ʿAbdullah ibn al-Zubayr reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “One suckling and two sucklings do not make marriage unlawful through breastfeeding.”"],[426,"ʿAbdullah ibn al-Zubayr reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no breastfeeding that counts except that which fills the stomach.”"],[427,"Ibn Abbas narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “This and this are equal,” meaning the little finger and the thumb are equal. “The teeth are equal as well; the front tooth and the molar are equal. This and this are equal.”"],[428,"Abu Musa al-Ashari narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The fingers are equal: ten camels for each one.”"],[429,"Rafiʿ ibn Khadij said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no cutting of the hand for stolen fruit or palm pith.”"],[430,"ʿA’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Overlook the slips of people of dignity, except in the prescribed punishments.”"],[431,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the slave steals, then sell him even for a Nish.”"],[432,"Ibn ʿAbbas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not take anything that has a soul as a target.”"],[433,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAbbas said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead goat and said: “What harm would there be upon its owners if they benefited from its hide?”"],[434,"ʿA’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A household that has dates does not go hungry.”"],[435,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Avoid wine, for it is the key to every evil.”"],[436,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wine is from these two trees: the palm tree and the grapevine.”"],[437,"Ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is wine.”"],[438,"Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “I forbid you from a small amount of that which intoxicates in large amounts.”"],[439,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade mixing unripe dates with dates, and raisins with dates."],[440,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Make things easy and do not make things difficult; calm people and do not repel them.”"],[441,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “Religion is sincere counsel.” He said: We said: “For whom, Messenger of Allah?” He said: “For Allah, His Messenger, His Book, the leaders of the Muslims, and their common people.”"],[442,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If allegiance is pledged to two caliphs, then kill the latter of them.”"],[443,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “People follow Quraysh in good and in evil.”"],[444,"ʿAbdullah ibn Abi Awfa narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And know that Paradise is beneath the shades of swords.”"],[445,"Abu al-Darda’ said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Seek for me your weak ones, for you are only provided for and granted victory through your weak ones.”"],[446,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The fighter has his reward, and the one who provides payment has his reward and the reward of the fighter.”"],[447,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The martyr is forgiven every sin except debt.”"],[448,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr.”"],[449,"Abu Fatimah said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that I may remain steadfast upon and do.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Hold fast to migration, for there is nothing like it.”"],[450,"Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah creates every maker and what he makes.”"],[451,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm.”"],[452,"Al-Barāʾ reported: The Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥassān: “Satirize them—or engage them in poetic combat—for Gabriel is with you.”"],[453,"Asmāʾ bint Yazīd reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I do not shake hands with women when accepting the pledge.”"],[454,"Buraydah reported: Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, each proposed marriage to Fāṭimah, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “She is young.” Then ʿAlī proposed to her, and the Prophet ﷺ married her to him."],[455,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I certainly joke, but I say nothing except the truth.”"],[456,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Caesar, saying: “If you turn away, you will bear the sin of the Arīsiyyīn.”"],[457,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise.”"],[458,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: The Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥassān: “Satirize them—or wage verbal battle against them—and Jibrīl (Gabriel) is with you.”"],[459,"Abū Ḥabbah al-Badrī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Abū Sufyān ibn al-Ḥārith is the best of my family.”"],[460,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man from among the Anṣār.”"],[461,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and addressed him: “O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “You are the people of our countryside, and we are the people of your town.”"],[462,"Anas ibn Mālik said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Faith is Yemeni, extending in this direction toward Lakhm and Judhām.”"],[463,"Jābir ibn Samurah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah, the Exalted, has named Madinah Ṭābah.”"],[464,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This Mount Uḥud is a mountain that loves us, and we love it.”"],[465,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people who were afflicted and said: “Why did these people not ask Allah for well-being?”"],[466,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī narrated that on the Day of Uḥud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive my people, for they do not know.”"],[467,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prompt your dying people to say: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.’”"],[468,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in his talbiyah: “Here I am at Your service, O Allah of truth, here I am.”"],[469,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I repent seventy times each day.”"],[470,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Truffles are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[471,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fever is from the intense heat of Hell, so extinguish it with water.”"],[472,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Fever is from the intense heat of Hell, so cool it with water.”"],[473,"Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Fever is from the intense heat of Hell, so cool it with water.”"],[474,"Al-Sā’ib ibn Yazīd, the nephew of Namir, narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no independent contagion, no Ṣafar, and no hāmah.”"],[475,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no Ṣafar, no hāmah, and no independent contagion.”"],[476,"Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me.”"],[477,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not one of us who does not recite the Qur’an melodiously.”"],[478,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not one of us who does not recite the Qur’an melodiously.”"],[479,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever masters the first seven sūrahs is a learned scholar.”"],[480,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Beware of corrupted relations between people, for they are the shaver.”"],[481,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Truffles are from the manna, and their liquid is a cure for the eye.”"],[482,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir said: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, has Sūrat al-Ḥajj been distinguished by containing two prostrations?” He replied: “Yes. Whoever does not perform both prostrations should not recite them.”"],[483,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Make matters easy and do not make them difficult. Give glad tidings and do not drive people away.”"],[484,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A fornicator who has received the prescribed punishment should not marry anyone except someone like him.”"],[485,"Al-Barāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥassān: “Satirize them—or answer their satire—and Gabriel is with you.”"],[486,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prompt your dying people to say: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.’”"],[487,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every sin of the martyr is forgiven except debt.”"],[488,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the falsest of speech…”"],[489,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I and the Hour have been sent like these two.” Meaning two fingers."],[490,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I have been sent, and the Hour is like these two.” Meaning two fingers."],[491,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Overlook the slips of people of dignity and good standing, except in matters involving prescribed legal punishments.”"],[492,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it.”"],[493,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not dislike daughters, for they are affectionate companions and precious.”"],[494,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, which expression of Islam is best?” He replied: “That of the person from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[495,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us.”"],[496,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us.”"],[497,"Iyās ibn Salamah narrated from his father that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us.”"],[498,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is innocent-hearted and noble, while the wicked person is deceitful and ignoble.”"],[499,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man should not sit between another man and his son.”"],[500,"Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Bite the meat directly from the bone, for that is more wholesome and more pleasant.”"],[501,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Free the captive, respond to the invitation, and visit the sick.”"],[502,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you dress and when you perform wuḍūʾ, begin with your right sides.”"],[503,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about poetry. He replied: “It is speech. What is good in it is good, and what is ugly in it is ugly.”"],[504,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Make things easy and do not make them difficult. Calm people and do not drive them away.”"],[505,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There should be no staying up at night except for one engaged in prayer or a traveler.”"],[506,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A lone rider is a devil, two riders are two devils, and three are a traveling group.”"],[507,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.”"],[508,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “Whoever is turned back by a superstitious omen has fallen into shirk.”"],[509,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a person of utmost truthfulness to be someone who frequently curses.”"],[510,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a believer to be someone who frequently curses.”"],[511,"ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man were to drag himself upon his face from the day he was born until the day he died of old age, seeking the pleasure of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, he would still regard that deed as insignificant on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[512,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Differ from the polytheists: let the beards grow and trim the mustaches closely.”"],[513,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Clip the mustaches, let the beards grow, and differ from the Magians.”"],[514,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Jews and Christians do not dye their hair, so differ from them.”"],[515,"Ḥafṣah narrated: ʿUṭārid ibn Ḥājib arrived with a brocade garment that Kisrā had given him. ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, why not buy it?” He replied: “It is worn only by one who has no share in the Hereafter.”"],[516,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached, the woman who tattoos and the one who has herself tattooed.”"],[517,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The woman is ʿawrah, and when she goes out, Satan seeks to make her appear attractive.”"],[518,"Thawbān narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What I fear most for my Ummah is the misguiding leaders.”"],[519,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I and the Hour have been sent like these two.” Meaning two fingers."],[520,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Before the Hour there will be transformation, the earth swallowing people, and stones being cast down.”"],[521,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Kaʿbah will be destroyed by the man with the two thin legs from Abyssinia.”"],[522,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Mahdī will be from my descendants, from the children of Fāṭimah.”"],[523,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires.”"],[524,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Fire has been veiled by desires, and Paradise has been veiled by hardships.”"],[525,"Abū Ṭalḥah may Allah be pleased with him, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.”"],[526,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row.”"],[527,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the prophets’ eyes sleep, but their hearts do not sleep.”"],[528,"Ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A prophet’s eyes sleep, but his heart does not sleep.”"],[529,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, I am the last of the prophets, and my mosque is the last of the mosques.”"],[530,"Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, ahead of you is a Basin whose extent is like the distance between Jarbāʾ and Adhruḥ.”"],[531,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man will indeed intercede for two or three people, and a man will intercede for one person.”"],[532,"Abū al-Dardāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The martyr will be permitted to intercede for seventy members of his household.”"],[533,"Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every servant will be resurrected upon the state in which he died.”"],[534,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Disputation concerning Divine Decree was delayed until the worst people of this Ummah.”"],[535,"Abū al-Dardāʾ may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Provision seeks the servant just as his appointed death seeks him.”"],[536,"Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will hear, and others will hear from you, and others will hear from those who heard from you.”"],[537,"Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[538,"Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: When the Prophet ﷺ entered the toilet, he would say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.”"],[539,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should rise for prayer while he is suffering from the need to relieve himself.”"],[540,"Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Keep to the siwāk, for it makes the mouth pleasant and is a means of pleasing the Lord.”"],[541,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would cause hardship for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk.”"],[542,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The key to prayer is purification; its commencement that makes ordinary actions prohibited is the takbīr, and its conclusion that makes them permissible again is the taslīm.”"],[543,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you perform wuḍūʾ, wash between the fingers of your hands and the toes of your feet.”"],[544,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No wuḍūʾ is required except because of a sound or an odor.”"],[545,"‘Abdullah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As reported that a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, the callers to prayer surpass us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say what they say, and when you finish, ask— and you will be given.”"],[546,"Abu Qatadah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the prayer is started, do not stand until you see me.”"],[547,"‘Ubadah ibn al-Samit reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no prayer for the one who does not recite the Opening of the Book.”"],[548,"Abu al-‘Aliyah said: Someone who heard the Prophet ﷺ told me that he said: “Give each surah its share of bowing and prostration.”"],[549,"‘Abd al-Rahman ibn ‘Awf reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row.”"],[550,"Al-Nu‘man ibn Bashir said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “You must straighten your rows, or Allah will cause discord between your faces.” In Muslim’s narration: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten our rows as if he were straightening arrow-shafts… then one day he came out and stood, about to begin, and he saw a man whose chest was protruding out of the row, so he said: “Servants of Allah, you must straighten your rows, or Allah will cause discord between your faces.” Abu Dawud narrates: “Straighten your rows” three times… “By Allah, you will straighten your rows or Allah will cause discord between your hearts.” He said: I saw a man pressing his shoulder to his companion’s shoulder, his knee to his companion’s knee, and his heel to his companion’s heel. And in another authentic narration: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would straighten our rows when we stood for prayer; once we were straight, he would say “Allāhu akbar.”"],[551,"‘A’ishah said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “If dinner is served and the prayer is established, then begin with dinner.”"],[552,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When the prayer is established, there is no (other) prayer except the obligatory one.”"],[553,"Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent your women from the mosques, though their houses are better for them.”"],[554,"‘A’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The two units before the dawn prayer are better than the world and everything in it.” In another narration: “They are more beloved to me than the entire world.”"],[555,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “When the prayer has been commenced, there is no prayer except the obligatory one.”"],[556,"Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah have mercy on a person who prays four units before ‘Asr.”"],[557,"Sabrah ibn Ma‘bad al-Juhani reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you prays, let him take a sutrah for his prayer—even if it is just an arrow.”"],[558,"‘A’ishah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah does not accept the prayer of a woman who has reached menstruating age unless she wears a head-covering (khimar).”"],[559,"Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not pray facing graves, and do not sit on them.”"],[560,"Masruq said: I asked ‘A’ishah about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said: Seven, nine, and eleven (rak‘ahs), not counting the two rak‘ahs of Fajr."],[561,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship (mosques).”"],[562,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let one of you pray in his (own) mosque, and do not go chasing after (different) mosques.”"],[563,"Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not make the mosques into thoroughfares, except for remembrance (of Allah) or prayer.”"],[564,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The ghusl of Friday is obligatory upon every adult (who has reached puberty).”"],[565,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah intends good for someone, He afflicts him with trials.”"],[566,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Visit the sick, and walk with funerals; they will remind you of the Hereafter.”"],[567,"ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prompt your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah.”"],[568,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of your garments are the white ones, so shroud your dead in them and wear them.”"],[569,"ʿĀ’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When your companion dies, leave him alone and do not speak badly of him.”"],[570,"Abū Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you pray over the deceased, then make your supplication sincerely for him.”"],[571,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “A miscarried child is to be prayed over, and supplication is made for its parents for forgiveness and mercy.”"],[572,"Abū Marthad al-Ghanawī said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not sit on graves, and do not pray toward them.”"],[573,"The Mother of the Believers, ‘A’ishah, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The charities of the desert people are to be taken at their watering places and in their courtyards.”"],[574,"Zaynab, the wife of ʿAbdullah, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give charity, O women, even if it is from your jewelry.”"],[575,"Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Part of the right due upon camels is that they be milked at the watering place.”"],[576,"Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, freed a slave-girl of hers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “If you had given her to some of your maternal uncles, that would have been greater in reward for you.”"],[577,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks while possessing the value of one uqiyyah has begged persistently.”"],[578,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks while having forty dirhams is one who begs persistently.”"],[579,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no obligatory charity due upon a slave except the charity of breaking the fast.”"],[580,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was taking the pre-dawn meal, and he said: “It is a blessing that Allah has given you, so do not abandon it.”"],[581,"Al-Miqdam ibn Maʿdi Karib reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hold firmly to the morning meal of the pre-dawn time, for it is the blessed morning meal.”"],[582,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Saʿidi reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people will remain upon goodness so long as they hasten the breaking of the fast.”"],[583,"Sinan ibn Sannah al-Aslami, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The grateful eater has a reward like the reward of the patient fasting person.”"],[584,"ʿA’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies while owing fasting, his guardian should fast on his behalf.”"],[585,"Ibn ʿUmar reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whoever seeks it should seek it in the last ten nights.”"],[586,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The striving of the elderly, the young, the weak, and the woman is pilgrimage and ʿumrah.”"],[587,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive the pilgrim and whoever the pilgrim seeks forgiveness for.”"],[588,"Ibn Umar reported from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “A person in ihram must not marry, give another in marriage, or make a marriage proposal.”"],[589,"Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibril came to me and commanded me to proclaim the talbiyah openly.”"],[590,"Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Wiping the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner causes sins to fall away completely.”"],[591,"Al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The emigrant may stay in Makkah for three nights after completing his rites.”"],[592,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “The best earning is the earning of a worker’s own hand when he is sincere.”"],[593,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The neighbor of a house has more right to the house of his neighbor, or the land.”"],[594,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give the worker his wages before his sweat dries.”"],[595,"Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever encloses land with a wall, it belongs to him.”"],[596,"Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The soul of the believer remains suspended as long as a debt remains upon him.”"],[597,"Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Allah does not accept the prayer of a mature woman except with a head covering.”"],[598,"Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A pledge is not forfeited; its gain belongs to its owner, and its liability is upon him.”"],[599,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A dinar for a dinar, and a dirham for a dirham, with no excess between them.”"],[600,"Uthman ibn Affan reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not sell one dinar for two dinars, nor one dirham for two dirhams.”"],[601,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Surplus water must not be withheld in order to prevent access to pasture.”"],[602,"Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever buys food should not sell it until he has fully taken possession of it.”"],[603,"Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “If you buy food, do not sell it until you have fully taken possession of it.”"],[604,"Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the most hated of men to Allah is the stubborn, fiercely argumentative opponent.”"],[605,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The inheritance of the child of li‘ān belongs to his mother and to her heirs after her.”"],[606,"Anas narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The freedman of a people is one of them,” or words to that effect."],[607,"Anas ibn Malik narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The son of a people’s sister is one of them,” or “from their own selves.”"],[608,"Usamah ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.”"],[609,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This world is a temporary enjoyment, and the best enjoyment of this world is a righteous woman.”"],[610,"Abu Hurayrah said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman should not lie in close bodily contact with another woman, and a man should not lie in close bodily contact with another man.”"],[611,"Ibn ‘Abbas said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man should not lie in close bodily contact with another man, and a woman should not lie in close bodily contact with another woman.”"],[612,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah curse those who have intercourse with women in their anuses.”"],[613,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you about the billy goat hired for use?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “It is the muhallil. Allah has cursed the muhallil and the one for whom it is done.”"],[614,"ʿA’ishah, the Mother of the Believers, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Breastfeeding makes unlawful what birth makes unlawful.”"],[615,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is appointed as a judge has been slaughtered without a knife.”"],[616,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: The Prophet ﷺ said, “The first matter to be judged among people will be bloodshed.”"],[617,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is going to swear, let him swear by Allah or remain silent.”"],[618,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever swears and says: ‘If Allah wills,’ has made an exception, so there is no breaking of the oath upon him.”"],[619,"Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man has no vow regarding what he does not own.”"],[620,"Umm Kurz said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For a boy, two sheep; and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[621,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Eating every predator with fangs is forbidden.”"],[622,"Usayd ibn Hudayr narrated that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, you appointed so-and-so but did not appoint me.” He said: “After me, you will see favoritism, so be patient until you meet me.”"],[623,"Muʿawiyah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies without a leader dies a death of the age of ignorance.”"],[624,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An unbeliever and the one who killed him will never be gathered together in the Fire.”"],[625,"Abu Umamah narrated that a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, permit me to travel in spiritual wandering.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “The spiritual journey of my nation is jihad in the path of Allah.”"],[626,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not wish to meet the enemy, but when you meet them, be steadfast.”"],[627,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Goodness is in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[628,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAbbas said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group shooting arrows and said: “Shoot, O sons of Ismaʿil, for your father was an archer.”"],[629,"Anas narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known.”"],[630,"Abu al-Darda’ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The martyr will be allowed to intercede for seventy of his family.”"],[631,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the night he was taken on the Night Journey and said: “Musa was brown-skinned and tall, as though he were from the men of Shanu’ah.”"],[632,"Abū Qatādah said: A Bedouin said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about fasting on Monday?” He said: “That is the day on which I was born, and on which revelation was sent down to me.”"],[633,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ spoke while he was in a tent on the Day of Badr, and he mentioned the supplication."],[634,"Anas was asked, “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye his hair?” He replied, “Only a small amount of white hair was visible on him.”"],[635,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not show mercy to one who does not show mercy to people.”"],[636,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, strengthen Islam specifically through ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[637,"Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard a man say: “O son of the close disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!” He replied: “If you are addressing someone from the family of al-Zubayr, then yes; otherwise, no.”"],[638,"Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah will enter the Fire.”"],[639,"Ibn Abī Awfā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah will enter the Fire.”"],[640,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw Jaʿfar flying in Paradise with the angels.”"],[641,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook at the death of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh.”"],[642,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays—meaning al-Ashʿarī—has been given one of the melodious voices of the family of Dāwūd.”"],[643,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah forgive Ghifār, and may Allah keep Aslam safe.”"],[644,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah keep Aslam safe, and may Allah forgive Ghifār.”"],[645,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah keep Aslam safe, and may Allah forgive Ghifār.”"],[646,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “It is not lawful for any one of you to carry weapons in Makkah.”"],[647,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The most beloved of all lands to Allah is the Sacred City.”"],[648,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you asks, let him ask abundantly, for he is asking his Lord.”"],[649,"Anas narrated: When the Prophet ﷺ entered the lavatory, he would say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.”"],[650,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prompt those among you who are nearing death to say: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.’”"],[651,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you perform the funeral prayer over the deceased, supplicate sincerely for him.”"],[652,"Ziyād ibn ʿIlāqah narrated from his uncle: The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, keep me away from reprehensible character, desires, deeds, and diseases.”"],[653,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I ask You for guidance, mindfulness of You, chastity, and freedom from need.”"],[654,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You in the best manner.”"],[655,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every child of Adam repeatedly commits errors, and the best of those who commit errors are those who repeatedly repent.”"],[656,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Glad tidings are for the one who finds abundant seeking of forgiveness recorded in his book of deeds.”"],[657,"ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no ruqyah more appropriate than ruqyah for the evil eye or a venomous sting.”"],[658,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no ruqyah more appropriate than ruqyah for the evil eye or a venomous sting.”"],[659,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Use antimony, for it clears the eyesight and causes the eyelashes to grow.”"],[660,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no independent contagion and no hāmah. Who, then, infected the first one?”"],[661,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Mother of the Qur’an is the Seven Oft-Repeated Verses and the Magnificent Qur’an.”"],[662,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah intends good for someone, He afflicts him with trials.”"],[663,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most hated of men in the sight of Allah is the fiercely argumentative opponent.”"],[664,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: When the verse: “Allah will bring forth a people whom He loves and who love Him” was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They are the people of this man,” meaning Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī."],[665,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not wish to meet the enemy, but when you meet them, remain steadfast.”"],[666,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The hoarded treasure of one of you will become a bald-headed, venomous male snake on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[667,"Abū Umāmah narrated: A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, permit me to wander through the land in religious seclusion.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “The religious journeying of my nation is striving in the path of Allah.”"],[668,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Mother of the Qur’an is the seven oft-repeated verses and the magnificent Qur’an.”"],[669,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, supplicate against the polytheists.” He replied: “I was not sent as one who curses. I was sent only as a mercy.”"],[670,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prostrated during Sūrat Ṣād and said: “David, peace be upon him, performed this prostration as repentance, while we perform it as gratitude.”"],[671,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse time, for Allah is the disposer of time.”"],[672,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah says: “Might is My garment and greatness is My cloak. Whoever contends with Me regarding either of them, I will punish him.”"],[673,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb delivered a sermon at al-Jābiyah and said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once stood among us just as I am standing among you and said: ‘…Whoever is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed is a believer.’”"],[674,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The two rakʿahs before Fajr are better than the world and everything in it.”"],[675,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Sūrat Tabārak is the protector from the punishment of the grave.”"],[676,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “One of them will stand in his sweat until it reaches halfway up his ears.”"],[677,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The time for the Maghrib prayer lasts as long as the twilight glow has not disappeared.”"],[678,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “‘Say: He is Allah, One’ is equivalent to one-third of the Qur’an.”"],[679,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every religion has a distinctive character, and the distinctive character of this religion is modesty.”"],[680,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.”"],[681,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.”"],[682,"Al-Ashʿath ibn Qays narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.”"],[683,"ʿUrwah narrated: ʿĀ’ishah was asked: “What did the Prophet ﷺ do in his home?” She replied: “He did what any one of you does: he repaired his sandal and patched his garment.”"],[684,"Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you loves his brother, let him tell him that he loves him.”"],[685,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[686,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A believer is not stung from the same hole twice.”"],[687,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, I declare inviolable the rights of the two weak ones: the orphan and the woman.”"],[688,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people most deserving of closeness to Allah are those who begin by giving salām.”"],[689,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand.”"],[690,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When dinner has been served and the prayer is commenced, begin with dinner.”"],[691,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: Abū Ḥumayd brought a cup of milk from al-Naqīʿ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Why did you not cover it, even if only by placing a stick across it?”"],[692,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days, and whatever exceeds that is charity.”"],[693,"Abū Qatādah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not curse time, for Allah is the One who controls time.”"],[694,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not call grapes ‘karm,’ for true nobility is in the heart of the believer.”"],[695,"Wā’il ibn Ḥujr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not call it al-karm. Rather, call it grapes or al-ḥabalah.”"],[696,"Abū al-Bakhtarī narrated: Someone who heard it directly from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me that he said: “The people will not be destroyed until they leave no excuse for themselves.”"],[697,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not leave fire burning in your homes when you go to sleep.”"],[698,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep your courtyards clean, for the Jews do not keep their courtyards clean.”"],[699,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī—or Abū Hurayrah—narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When three people set out on a journey, let them appoint one of them as their leader.”"],[700,"Ḍamrah ibn Thaʿlabah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People will continue to remain upon goodness so long as they do not envy one another.”"],[701,"Abū Khirāsh al-Sulamī narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever boycotts his brother for a year, it is like shedding his blood.”"],[702,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, supplicate against the polytheists.” He replied: “I was not sent as one who curses. I was only sent as a mercy.”"],[703,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Might is His lower garment, and greatness is His cloak; whoever contends with Me regarding them, I will punish him.”"],[704,"Hishām ibn Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah will punish those who torture people in this world.”"],[705,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a two-faced person to be trustworthy.”"],[706,"Asmāʾ bint Yazīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you who the best among you are?” They replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered.” Then he said: “Shall I tell you who the worst among you are? Those who go about spreading malicious gossip, those who cause corruption between people who love one another, and those who seek hardship and ruin for the innocent.”"],[707,"Kaʿb ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Every nation has a particular trial, and the trial of my Ummah is wealth.”"],[708,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man’s true nobility is his religion, his manly virtue is his intelligence, and his distinction is his character.”"],[709,"Zayd ibn Arqam narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not trim his mustache is not from us.”"],[710,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Change the gray hair, and do not imitate the Jews or the Christians.”"],[711,"Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated: I asked Anas ibn Mālik: “Did the Prophet ﷺ dye his hair?” He replied: “He had only a small amount of gray hair.”"],[712,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A woman asked: “O Messenger of Allah, may I say that my husband gave me something he did not actually give me?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood.”"],[713,"Zaynab, the wife of ʿAbdullāh, narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “If one of you attends the mosque, she should not apply perfume.”"],[714,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Do not return after me to disbelief, striking one another’s necks.”"],[715,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar mentioned the Ḥarūriyyah and said that the Prophet ﷺ said: “They will pass out of Islam just as an arrow passes through its target.”"],[716,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “I and the Hour were sent together; it nearly preceded me.”"],[717,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Before the Hour, usury, adultery, and wine will become widespread.”"],[718,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The House will certainly continue to be visited for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah even after the emergence of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj.”"],[719,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Hour will not be established until the House is no longer visited for Ḥajj.”"],[720,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Hour will be established only upon the worst of people.”"],[721,"ʿAlbāʾ al-Sulamī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will be established only upon the dregs of mankind.”"],[722,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Dajjāl will emerge from here,” and he pointed toward the East."],[723,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The House will certainly continue to be visited for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah even after the emergence of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj.”"],[724,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection while the sky is drizzling upon them.”"],[725,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Every servant will be resurrected upon the state in which he died.”"],[726,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās heard the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon and saying: “You will meet Allah walking, barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.”"],[727,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Day of Resurrection will be like the length of time between Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr.”"],[728,"Abū Umāmah narrated: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh?” He replied: “People being driven toward Paradise bound together in chains.”"],[729,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People whose hearts are like the hearts of birds will enter Paradise.”"],[730,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Faith consists of sixty-something branches, and modesty is a branch of faith.”"],[731,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Worship the Most Merciful, spread the greeting of peace, and feed people; you will enter the Gardens of Paradise.”"],[732,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Allah will bring some people out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise.”"],[733,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms.”"],[734,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A sign of faith is love for the Anṣār, and a sign of hypocrisy is hatred for the Anṣār.”"],[735,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Anṣār.”"],[736,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Anṣār.”"],[737,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, having good expectations of Allah is part of excellent worship of Allah.”"],[738,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a man says to his brother, ‘O disbeliever,’ then one of the two has incurred it.”"],[739,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah is amazed at a people who will enter Paradise in chains.”"],[740,"Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, while the funeral bier was laid before him — meaning that of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh: “The Throne of al-Raḥmān shook for him.”"],[741,"Muʿādh ibn Jabal may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be beneath the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[742,"Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: Jibrīl promised the Prophet ﷺ that he would come to him. He said: “We do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog.”"],[743,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or images.”"],[744,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a dog or a bell.”"],[745,"ʿĀʾishah may Allah be pleased with her reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O ʿĀʾishah, indeed my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep.”"],[746,"Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, my intercession on the Day of Resurrection is for those from my Ummah who committed major sins.”"],[747,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī, may Allah be pleased with them, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, three days before his death, say: “Let none of you die except while having a good expectation of Allah.”"],[748,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A person does not believe until he believes in Divine Decree—its good and its evil.”"],[749,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The two eyes commit zinā, the two hands commit zinā, the two feet commit zinā, and the private part commits zinā.”"],[750,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah intends good for, He grants understanding in the religion.”"],[751,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion.”"],[752,"ʿAwf ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No one should give public exhortation except a ruler, one who has been authorized to do so, or an arrogant person.”"],[753,"ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one should give public exhortation except a ruler, one who has been authorized to do so, or one who takes it upon himself without proper right or qualification.”"],[754,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the Children of Israel wrote a book, then followed it and abandoned the Torah.”"],[755,"Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and began speaking eloquently. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some eloquent speech is like magic, and indeed some poetry contains wisdom.”"],[756,"Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: “What prevents me from narrating many ḥadīths to you is that the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him take his seat in the Fire.’”"],[757,"Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take a house in the Fire.”"],[758,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[759,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is sufficient as a lie for a person to narrate everything he hears.”"],[760,"ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no prayer in the presence of food, nor while one is resisting the urge of the two foul things.”"],[761,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of the two acts that bring curses.” It was asked: “What are the two acts that bring curses, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “One who relieves himself in the people’s roadway or in their shade.”"],[762,"Jabir said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Between a person and shirk and kufr is abandoning the prayer.”"],[763,"Rafi‘ ibn Khadij said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pray the dawn prayer when morning becomes clear, for that is greater for your reward.”"],[764,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Delay the noon prayer until it cools, for the intensity of heat is from the blazing breath of Hell.”"],[765,"Safwan ibn Makhramah al-Zuhri reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Delay the noon prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the blazing breath of Hell.”"],[766,"Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever misses the ‘Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth.”"],[767,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever catches one unit of a prayer has caught the prayer.” In another narration in Muslim: “Whoever catches one unit of the prayer with the imam has caught one unit.”"],[768,"‘A’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in his bowing and prostration: “Perfectly Glorious, Perfectly Pure—Lord of the angels and the Spirit.”"],[769,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If they are three, then let one of them lead them. The one most entitled to lead is the one who recites best.”"],[770,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of establishing the prayer.”"],[771,"Anas said: The prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to face us and said: “Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I can see you from behind my back.” In a narration in al-Bukhari: One of us would press his shoulder to his companion’s shoulder and his foot to his companion’s foot. In ‘Abd al-Razzaq’s narration: “Keep checking these rows, for I can see you from behind me.”"],[772,"Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari came to Madinah and was asked: “What have you found changed in us since the days you knew the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “I have not found anything changed except that you do not straighten the rows.”"],[773,"‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prayer in congregation surpasses praying alone by twenty-seven degrees.”"],[774,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Congregational prayer surpasses praying alone by twenty-five degrees.”"],[775,"‘A’ishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Prayer is not (to be performed) when food is present, nor while one is being pressed by the two filthy matters (i.e., needing to relieve himself).”"],[776,"Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “If one of you attends the ‘Isha prayer, then let her not apply perfume that night.”"],[777,"‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Make some of your prayer in your houses, and do not take them as graves.”"],[778,"‘Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no obligatory prayer except that before it are two units.”"],[779,"Abu Hurayrah said: “I testify that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever prays in a single garment, let him bring its two ends in opposite directions (i.e., arrange it so it properly covers him and is secured).’”"],[780,"‘Uqbah ibn ‘Amir al-Juhani said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who recites the Qur’an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly, and the one who recites the Qur’an quietly is like the one who gives charity secretly.”"],[781,"Abu Sa‘id narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever reaches Fajr without having prayed Witr, then there is no Witr for him.”"],[782,"Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Hour will not be established until people compete/boast with one another regarding mosques.”"],[783,"Khuzaymah ibn Thābit reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever eats from this herb should not come near our mosque.”"],[784,"Abū Hurayrah reported the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every sermon in which there is no tashahhud is like a severed hand.”"],[785,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever catches one rakʿah of the prayer has caught the prayer.”"],[786,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever catches one rakʿah of the Friday prayer has caught it.”"],[787,"The Mother of the Believers, ʿĀ’ishah, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Fever causes sins to fall away just as a tree drops its leaves.”"],[788,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ, three days before his death, say: “Let none of you die except while having a good opinion of Allah.”"],[789,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, when death approached him, called for new clothes and put them on. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The deceased will be resurrected in the clothes in which he dies.”"],[790,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not pray for a wailing woman nor for a woman who shrieks loudly.”"],[791,"Umm ʿAṭiyyah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the washing of his daughter: “Begin with her right side and the parts of her body used for ablution.”"],[792,"Umm ʿAṭiyyah said: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us while we were washing his daughter and said: “Put camphor, or some camphor, in the final wash.”"],[793,"Abū Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “If one hundred Muslims pray over him, he is forgiven.”"],[794,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No people withhold zakat except that Allah afflicts them with years of hardship.”"],[795,"Umm Salamah said: I used to wear gold ornaments, so I said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, is this considered hoarded wealth?” He said: “Whatever reaches the amount on which zakat is due, and its zakat is paid, is not hoarded wealth.”"],[796,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you pay the zakat of your wealth, you have fulfilled what is due upon you.”"],[797,"Umm Salamah said: I used to wear gold jewelry and asked: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, is this considered hoarded wealth? He said: “Whatever reaches the amount on which zakat is due and its zakat is paid is not considered hoarded wealth.”"],[798,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no zakat on less than five awsuq of dates.”"],[799,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the collector comes to you, let him not leave except while he is pleased.”"],[800,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Eat, give charity, and dress yourselves, without extravagance and without arrogance.”"],[801,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for one who is strong and sound.”"],[802,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and physically sound.”"],[803,"A man from Banu Hilal said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Charity is not suitable for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and sound.”"],[804,"Hubshi ibn Junadah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks without being poor, it is as though he is eating burning coals.”"],[805,"Abu Bakrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Two months do not decrease: the two months of the festivals, Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah.”"],[806,"ʿUthman ibn Abi al-ʿAs al-Thaqafi said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Fasting is a shield from the Fire, just like the shield one of you uses in battle.”"],[807,"Sahl ibn Saʿd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts the Day of ʿArafah will be forgiven for two consecutive years.”"],[808,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of continuous fasting, beware of continuous fasting.” They said: But you continue fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I am not like you. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"],[809,"Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman must not travel for three days unless she has a mahram with her.”"],[810,"Jabir ibn Abdullah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the hyena, and he said: “It is game.” A ram is required as compensation if a person in ihram hunts it."],[811,"‘Aishah menstruated at Sarif, then became pure at ‘Arafah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Your going between al-Safa and al-Marwah will suffice for both your Hajj and your ‘Umrah.”"],[812,"Ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep away from the bottom of ‘Uranah. Keep away from the bottom of Muhassir.”"],[813,"Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you stone the pillars, it will be a light for you on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[814,"Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Women are not required to shave; rather, women are only required to shorten their hair.”"],[815,"Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fever is from the heat of Hellfire, so cool it with Zamzam water.”"],[816,"Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The people used to depart in every direction, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one should depart until his last act is at the House.”"],[817,"Jabir was asked about riding the sacrificial offering, and he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Ride it in a proper manner when you are compelled to do so, until you find another mount.”"],[818,"Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, is there jihad upon women? He said: “Yes, upon them is a jihad in which there is no fighting: the pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage.”"],[819,"Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The standard for weight is the weight of the people of Makkah, and the standard for dry measure is the measure of the people of Madinah.”"],[820,"Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Banu al-Najjar, name a price for your garden,” and in it were ruined areas and date-palms."],[821,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever releases a Muslim from a sale, Allah will relieve his slip.” In another narration: “on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[822,"Rafi‘ ibn Khadij reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “The worst earnings are the payment of a prostitute, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a cupper.”"],[823,"Rafi‘ ibn Khadij said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The worst earnings are the payment of a prostitute, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a cupper.”"],[824,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you sells a sheep or a milch-camel, he must not withhold its milk in the udder in order to make it appear to contain more milk.”"],[825,"Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a date lying on the road and said: “Were it not that I fear it might be from charity, I would have eaten it.”"],[826,"Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes possession of lost property is astray so long as he does not announce it.”"],[827,"Ibn Masʿūd reported that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: “Respond to the one who invites you, do not reject a gift, and do not strike the Muslims.”"],[828,"Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wala’ is a bond like the bond of lineage: it is neither sold nor given away.”"],[829,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A bequest for an heir is not valid; the child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone [i.e., nothing].”"],[830,"Ibn ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Clientship is a bond like the bond of kinship; it is not to be sold and not to be gifted.”"],[831,"Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Every sermon in which there is no declaration of faith is like a severed hand.”"],[832,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most complete of the believers in faith are those best in character, and the best of you are the best of you to their women.”"],[833,"Jabir ibn ʿAbd Allah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Any slave who marries without the permission of his master is a fornicator.”"],[834,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “No man should be alone with a woman unless she has with her a mahram.”"],[835,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Three matters whose seriousness is serious and whose joking is serious: marriage, divorce, and taking back one’s wife.”"],[836,"ʿAbbas ibn Sahl, from his father, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAsim ibn ʿAdi: “Keep the woman with you until she gives birth.”"],[837,"Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the major sins. He said: “Associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, killing a soul, and bearing false witness.”"],[838,"Ibn Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one against whom the claim is made has more right to the oath unless proof is established.”"],[839,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you dispute concerning the road, its width is to be made seven cubits.”"],[840,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The greatest of the major sins are associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, and disobeying one’s parents.”"],[841,"Buraydah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The killing of a believer is greater in the sight of Allah than the passing away of the whole world.”"],[842,"Jabir reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no cutting of the hand for the betrayer, the plunderer, or the snatcher.”"],[843,"Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no cutting of the hand for the plunderer, the snatcher, or the betrayer.”"],[844,"Asma’ bint Yazid narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The birth sacrifice for a boy is two equal sheep, and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[845,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A boy was born to me tonight, and I named him with the name of my father Ibrahim.”"],[846,"Abu Zuhayr al-Numayri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill locusts, for they are an army from the armies of Allah.”"],[847,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the hyena, and he said: “It is game, and a ram is due for it if a person in the state of consecration hunts it.”"],[848,"ʿAbdullah ibn Busr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came as a guest to my father. He said: We brought near to him food and watbah, and he ate from it. The hadith."],[849,"Salma narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A house in which there are no dates is like a house in which there is no food.”"],[850,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A drink or meal in the evening, or a drink or meal in the morning, suffices for necessity.”"],[851,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “People from my nation will drink wine, calling it by a name other than its name.”"],[852,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden. Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is forbidden.”"],[853,"Abu Masʿud al-Ansari said: A man came with a she-camel that had a halter and said: “This is in the path of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Because of it, you will have seven hundred she-camels on the Day of Resurrection, all of them with halters.”"],[854,"Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No people abandon jihad except that Allah encompasses them with punishment.”"],[855,"Abu Musa al-Ashʿari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Free the suffering captive — meaning the prisoner — feed the hungry, and visit the sick.”"],[856,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sincerely seeks martyrdom will be granted it, even if it does not physically reach him.”"],[857,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “A woman may take protection for a people,” meaning she may grant protection binding upon the Muslims."],[858,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whoever says: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, has lied.”"],[859,"Al-Ḥārith ibn Mālik ibn al-Barṣāʾ reported: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “This city shall not be invaded after this day until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[860,"ʿĀ’ishah reported: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Which people are the best?” He replied: “The generation in which I live, then the second, and then the third.”"],[861,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has placed the truth upon ʿUmar’s tongue and in his heart.”"],[862,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: Mount Uḥud shook while the Prophet ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān were upon it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Be firm, Uḥud. Upon you are only a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.”"],[863,"Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who pledged allegiance beneath the Tree will enter the Fire.”"],[864,"Anas narrated from Umm Sulaym that she said: “O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your servant, so supplicate to Allah for him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in what You have given him.”"],[865,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of the martyrs in the sight of Allah is Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.”"],[866,"Anas ibn Mālik reported that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, while the funeral of Saʿd was laid before him: “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for him.”"],[867,"ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of the women of her time was Maryam, and the best of the women of her time was Khadījah bint Khuwaylid.”"],[868,"Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The superiority of ʿĀ’ishah over other women is like the superiority of tharīd over all other foods.”"],[869,"The Mother of the Believers, ʿĀ’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The superiority of ʿĀ’ishah over other women is like the superiority of tharīd over all other foods.”"],[870,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, You caused the first of Quraysh to taste punishment, so cause the last of them to taste generosity and bestowal.”"],[871,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Anṣār.”"],[872,"Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the descendants of the Anṣār, the descendants of their descendants, their freed servants, and their neighbors.”"],[873,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the children of the Anṣār, and the children of the children of the Anṣār.”"],[874,"Abū Ṭalḥah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Convey my greetings of peace to your people, for throughout the time I have known them, they have been chaste and patient.”"],[875,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no true life except the life of the Hereafter, so set right the Anṣār and the Muhājirūn.”"],[876,"Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr narrated that a man from the Anṣār said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint me to a position as you appointed so-and-so?” He replied: “After me, you will encounter others being preferred over you, so remain patient until you meet me at the Reservoir.”"],[877,"Fāṭimah bint Qays narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “This is Ṭaybah. This is Ṭaybah. This is Ṭaybah.” He meant Madinah. This forms part of the hadith."],[878,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The area between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise.”"],[879,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Supplication is not rejected between the adhān and the iqāmah, so supplicate.”"],[880,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah will send ten blessings upon him.”"],[881,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever neglects to send blessings upon me has missed the path to Paradise.”"],[882,"Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned, yet he does not send blessings upon me.”"],[883,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Nothing is more honorable before Allah, the Exalted, than supplication.”"],[884,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Supplication is not rejected between the call to prayer and the commencement of the prayer, so supplicate.”"],[885,"Anas narrated that Umm Sulaym said: “O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your servant, so supplicate to Allah for him.” He said: “O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in what You have given him.”"],[886,"Ḥudhayfah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ would say between the two prostrations: “My Lord, forgive me. My Lord, forgive me.”"],[887,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah accepts the repentance of His servant so long as his soul has not reached his throat.”"],[888,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever cauterizes himself or asks another to perform ruqyah for him has withdrawn from complete reliance upon Allah.”"],[889,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There are two blessings concerning which many people suffer loss: health and free time.”"],[890,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has not sent down an illness without also sending down its cure.”"],[891,"Abū Burdah ibn Qays, the brother of Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, make the death of my nation in Your cause occur through piercing wounds and plague.”"],[892,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no independent contagion, no hāmah, no attribution of rain to the stars, and no Ṣafar.”"],[893,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no Ṣafar, no hāmah, and a sick person does not independently infect a healthy person.”"],[894,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood.”"],[895,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to say: “Do not relate a dream except to a knowledgeable person or a sincere adviser.”"],[896,"Umm Ayyūb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Qur’an was revealed in seven modes. Whichever of them you recite will suffice you.”"],[897,"Jābir narrated: Three days before the Prophet ﷺ died, I heard him say: “None of you should die except while holding a good expectation of Allah.”"],[898,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Avoid the seven destructive sins.” Among them, he mentioned: “Unlawfully consuming the wealth of an orphan.”"],[899,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah accepts the repentance of His servant so long as the soul has not reached the throat.”"],[900,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person or a strong, able-bodied person.”"],[901,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah accepts the repentance of His servant as long as the soul has not reached the throat.”"],[902,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “What stands between a person and polytheism and disbelief is abandoning the prayer.”"],[903,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said concerning the words: “There is none of you except that he will reach it”: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All people will reach the Fire, and then they will depart from it according to their deeds.”"],[904,"Abū al-Zubayr narrated: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah being asked about riding a sacrificial animal. He replied: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Ride it in a reasonable manner when necessity compels you, until you find another mount.”"],[905,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is held back by his deeds will not be advanced by his lineage.”"],[906,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of two people is sufficient for three, and the food of three is sufficient for four.”"],[907,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the major sins. He replied: “Associating partners with Allah, disobeying one’s parents, killing a person, and giving false testimony.”"],[908,"Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned, yet he does not invoke blessings upon me.”"],[909,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever invokes one blessing upon me, Allah will send ten blessings upon him.”"],[910,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘I am better than Jonah son of Mattā,’ has spoken falsely.”"],[911,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Kinship is a closely intertwined bond. Whoever maintains it, I maintain ties with him, and whoever cuts it off, I cut him off.”"],[912,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Which people are the best?” He replied: “The generation in which I live, then the second, then the third.”"],[913,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is held back by his deeds will not be brought forward by his lineage.”"],[914,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first convulsion has come, followed by the second. Death has come with all that it contains.”"],[915,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, a man may attain through his good character the rank of one who stands in prayer during the night.”"],[916,"Jābir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When Allah intends good for a people, He brings gentleness among them.”"],[917,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness in every matter.”"],[918,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever shows mercy, even to an animal being slaughtered, Allah will show mercy to him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[919,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders.”"],[920,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to our young and show reverence to our elders is not of us.”"],[921,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A person follows the religion and way of his close friend, so let each of you carefully consider whom he takes as a close friend.”"],[922,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, among the highest forms of dutifulness is for a child to maintain ties with those whom his father loved.”"],[923,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders.”"],[924,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"],[925,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful conduct will not enter Paradise.”"],[926,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: When the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Welcome to the delegation who have come neither disgraced nor regretful…” to the end of the hadith."],[927,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man tells another person something and then looks around, it is a trust.”"],[928,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of two is sufficient for three, and the food of three is sufficient for four.”"],[929,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should drink while standing. Whoever forgets and does so should make himself vomit.”"],[930,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days, and anything beyond that is charity.”"],[931,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days, and whatever exceeds that is charity.”"],[932,"Abū Mūsā narrated: Abū al-Dardāʾ and I were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: “Whoever guards what is between his two jaws and what is between his two legs will enter Paradise.”"],[933,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and began speaking. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some eloquence is like magic, and some poetry contains wisdom.”"],[934,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ḥassān ibn Thābit: “Satirize them—or respond to their satire—and Jibrīl is with you.”"],[935,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If there are three people, two of them should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third.”"],[936,"Sahl ibn Ḥunayf narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My soul has become foul.’ Rather, let him say, ‘My soul feels unsettled.’”"],[937,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One bed is for the man, one bed is for his wife, the third is for the guest, and the fourth is for Satan.”"],[938,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a dog or a bell.”"],[939,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of the two acts that bring curses.” They asked: “What are the two acts that bring curses, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Relieving oneself in the road used by people or in the places where they seek shade.”"],[940,"Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever harms the Muslims on their roads deserves their curse.”"],[941,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If it were to be in anything, it would be in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling.” Meaning: misfortune or an evil omen."],[942,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “If it were to be in anything, it would be in the dwelling, the servant, and the horse.”"],[943,"Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib and Abū Umāmah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When a ruler goes looking for reasons to suspect people, he corrupts them.”"],[944,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seek help in accomplishing your needs by keeping them concealed, for every blessing has someone who envies it.”"],[945,"Saʿd ibn Mālik Abū Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days.”"],[946,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is enough of a lie for a person to relate everything he hears.”"],[947,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whatever two people who insult one another say, the burden falls upon the one who began it until the wronged person exceeds the limit.”"],[948,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Those who frequently curse will not be intercessors or witnesses on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[949,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The worst traits that can be in a man are overwhelming avarice and devastating cowardice.”"],[950,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not laugh excessively, for excessive laughter deadens the heart.”"],[951,"Qays ibn Saʿd said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Scheming and deception are in the Fire,” I would have been among the most cunning of people."],[952,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he noticed a group of people and asked: “Why have these people gathered?” It was said: “They are gathered around a grave they are digging.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became deeply alarmed and hurried ahead of his Companions until he reached the grave. He knelt beside it. I moved around in front of him so that I could see what he was doing. He wept until his tears wet the earth. Then he turned toward us and said: “O my brothers, prepare yourselves for a day like this.”"],[953,"Anas said: “You commit deeds that appear in your eyes to be finer than a hair, yet during the time of the Prophet ﷺ we used to count them among the destructive sins.” Abū ʿAbdullāh—meaning al-Bukhārī—said: “By this he means sins that lead to destruction.”"],[954,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.”"],[955,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Eat, give charity, and wear clothing without extravagance or arrogance.”"],[956,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whatever of the izār hangs below the ankles is in the Fire.”"],[957,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One bed is for the man, one bed is for his wife, the third is for the guest, and the fourth is for Satan.”"],[958,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “From the fiṭrah are shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails, and trimming the mustache.”"],[959,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Silk and gold are forbidden for the males of my Ummah and lawful for its females.”"],[960,"Abū Ṭalḥah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The angels do not enter a house containing a dog or images.”"],[961,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not enter a house containing statues or images.”"],[962,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever holds firmly to my Sunnah when my Ummah becomes corrupt will have the reward of a martyr.”"],[963,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs a deed that is not in accordance with our command, it is rejected.”"],[964,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not turn back after me as disbelievers, striking one another’s necks.”"],[965,"A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Leave the Abyssinians alone so long as they leave you alone, and leave the Turks alone so long as they leave you alone.”"],[966,"Abū Jubayrah ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk narrated from one of the men of the Anṣār that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I and the Hour were sent like these two, and I preceded it by only the breath of the Hour.”"],[967,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What will your condition be when Ibn Maryam descends among you while your imam is from among yourselves?”"],[968,"When death approached Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, he asked for new clothes and put them on. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The deceased will be resurrected in the clothes in which he dies.”"],[969,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, my intercession on the Day of Resurrection is for those among my Ummah who committed major sins.”"],[970,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever strikes another person unjustly will have retaliation exacted from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[971,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The construction of Paradise consists of a brick of gold and a brick of silver.”"],[972,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Sayḥān, Jayḥān, the Euphrates, and the Nile are all among the rivers of Paradise.”"],[973,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah marvels at people who enter Paradise in chains.”"],[974,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The poor among the Muhājirūn will enter Paradise five hundred years before their wealthy ones.”"],[975,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This fire is one part out of one hundred parts of Hell.”"],[976,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believers with the most complete faith are those with the best character, and the best of you are those who are best in character toward their wives.”"],[977,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself.”"],[978,"Yazīd ibn Asad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Yazīd ibn Asad, love for people what you love for yourself.”"],[979,"Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty and faith are joined together. When one of them is removed, the other is removed as well.”"],[980,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hardness of heart and roughness are in the east, while faith is among the people of the Ḥijāz.”"],[981,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Part of the excellence of a person’s Islam is that he leaves what does not concern him.”"],[982,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange just as it began. So glad tidings are for the strangers.”"],[983,"Ibn ʿUmar may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of the supplications of the oppressed, for they ascend to the heaven as though they were sparks.”"],[984,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The heart of the son of Adam is only between two fingers of al-Raḥmān.”"],[985,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or images.”"],[986,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “At the entrances of Madinah are angels. Neither the plague nor the Dajjāl will enter it.”"],[987,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and His angels send blessings upon the first row.”"],[988,"Anas may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever among you lives to meet Jesus son of Mary should convey to him my greetings of peace.”"],[989,"Abū al-Dardāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Those who frequently curse others will not be witnesses or intercessors on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[990,"Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them, said: The Prophet ﷺ forbade vows and said: “They do not repel anything. They only draw something out of the miser.”"],[991,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of people in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam when they gain understanding of the religion.”"],[992,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is given a religious verdict without knowledge, its sin is upon the one who gave him that verdict.”"],[993,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me shall enter the Fire.”"],[994,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a dog drinks from the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times.”"],[995,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ibrāhīm, peace be upon him, circumcised himself when he was eighty years old, using the qadūm.”"],[996,"A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would cause hardship for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk with every prayer.”"],[997,"Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim , may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for me, I pour water over my head three times.” He gestured with both hands."],[998,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The prayer of one of you is not accepted after he breaks his state of purification until he performs wuḍūʾ.”"],[999,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from ghulūl.”"],[1000,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No prayer is accepted without purification, nor charity from ghulūl.”"],[1001,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “My Ummah on the Day of Resurrection will have brightness from prostration and bright-marked limbs from wuḍūʾ.”"],[1002,"Khuzaymah ibn Thābit reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Wiping over the leather socks is for the traveler for three days, and for the resident for one day and one night.”"],[1003,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The imam is responsible, and the caller to prayer is entrusted. O Allah, guide the leaders of prayer and forgive the callers to prayer.”"],[1004,"Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The imam is responsible, and the caller to prayer is entrusted. O Allah, guide the leaders of prayer and forgive the callers to prayer.”"],[1005,"‘A’ishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every prayer in which the Mother of the Book is not recited is deficient.”"],[1006,"Anas ibn Malik reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like the spreading of a dog.”"],[1007,"The Mother of the Believers ‘A’ishah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you breaks ablution during his prayer, let him hold his nose and then leave.”"],[1008,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They lead you in prayer; if they are correct, it is for you; and if they err, it is for you and against them.”"],[1009,"‘Abdullah ibn Mas‘ud reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be brief in the prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs.”"],[1010,"Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be brief in the prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs.”"],[1011,"Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and His angels send blessings upon the first row.”"],[1012,"Zayd ibn Khalid reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unperfumed.”"],[1013,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any woman who has applied incense/perfume should not attend the ‘Isha (late-night) prayer with us.”"],[1014,"Abu Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it.”"],[1015,"Shaddad ibn Aws said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be different from the Jews, for they do not pray in their sandals or their leather socks (khuff).”"],[1016,"Sabrah ibn Ma‘bad al-Juhani reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not pray in the camel watering/resting places, but do pray in the sheep enclosure.”"],[1017,"‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O people of the Qur’an, pray Witr, for Allah is Witr and He loves Witr.”"],[1018,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought rain, he would say: “O Allah, give drink to Your servants and Your livestock, spread Your mercy, and revive Your dead land.”"],[1019,"Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rakʿahs before sitting down.”"],[1020,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever is in the mosque waiting for the prayer is considered to be in prayer.”"],[1021,"Jābir reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let none of you lie on his back and then place one of his legs over the other.”"],[1022,"Abū Mūsā reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A believer to another believer is like a building: each part strengthens the other,” and he interlaced his fingers."],[1023,"Nubayshah al-Hudhalī said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The days of Tashrīq are days of eating and drinking.” And in another narration, it adds: “and remembrance of Allah.”"],[1024,"Abū al-Dardā’ reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not eat while reclining, and do not step over people’s necks on Friday.”"],[1025,"Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you becomes drowsy on Friday, let him move from that seat.”"],[1026,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “How are you this morning?” He replied: “Better than people who did not visit a sick person and did not attend a funeral.”"],[1027,"Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah says: I am according to My servant’s opinion of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me.”"],[1028,"Jābir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you dies, if he has the means, let him be shrouded in a striped cloth.”"],[1029,"ʿĀ’ishah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not insult the dead, for they have already gone on to what they sent ahead.”"],[1030,"ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see a funeral, stand for it until it passes beyond you or is set down.”"],[1031,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Most of the punishment of the grave is because of urine, so protect yourselves from urine.”"],[1032,"Abū Ayyūb reported that a young boy was buried, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If anyone could have escaped the squeeze of the grave, this child would have escaped it.”"],[1033,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A Muslim owes no charity on his slave or on his horse.”"],[1034,"Jabir ibn Samurah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When Allah gives one of you something good, let him begin with himself and the people of his household.”"],[1035,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The fast is on the day you all fast, the breaking of the fast is on the day you all break it, and the sacrifice feast is on the day you all offer sacrifice.”"],[1036,"Hafsah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not make the intention for fasting during the night has no fast.”"],[1037,"ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal.”"],[1038,"Abu Musa al-Ashʿari reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts all year long, Hell will be narrowed around him like this,” and he gestured by forming ninety."],[1039,"Ibn ʿUmar said: A man saw that the Night of Decree was the night of the twenty-seventh. So the Prophet ﷺ said: “I see your dreams concerning the last ten nights, so seek it in the odd nights among them.”"],[1040,"Abu Hurairah said: We were discussing the Night of Decree in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Which of you remembers when the moon rose, and it was like half of a bowl?”"],[1041,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever reaches ‘Arafah before dawn rises has reached the pilgrimage.”"],[1042,"Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Establish the prayer, give the alms, perform the pilgrimage, perform the lesser pilgrimage, and be upright, and matters will be set right for you.”"],[1043,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The delay of a wealthy person in paying is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a solvent person, then let him follow that transfer.”"],[1044,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the Final Hour comes while one of you has a small palm shoot in his hand, then let him plant it.”"],[1045,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Delay in payment by one who is able to pay is injustice. If one of you is referred for payment to a solvent person, then let him accept the transfer.”"],[1046,"Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever finds the very property of his own with a man is more entitled to it.”"],[1047,"Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever deceives us is not from us, and whoever attacks us at night is not from us.”"],[1048,"Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Beware of excessive swearing in transactions, for it may make the merchandise sell, but afterward it erases the blessing.”"],[1049,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet said: “Return the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you.”"],[1050,"The Mother of the Believers, ‘A’ishah, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not sell your fruits until their ripeness appears and they are safe from blight.”"],[1051,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah destroy the Jews. Fat was forbidden to them, yet they sold it and consumed its price.”"],[1052,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that vomits and then returns to its vomit.”"],[1053,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give the prescribed shares to those who are entitled to them, and whatever remains goes to the nearest male relative.”"],[1054,"‘Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The wala’ is inherited by whoever inherits the wealth through a parent or a child.”"],[1055,"‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever frees a slave, Allah will free a limb of his for every limb of that slave.”"],[1056,"‘Uqbah ibn ‘Amir reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you made private relations lawful.”"],[1057,"Buraydah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What the people of this world regard as status is this wealth.”"],[1058,"Al-‘Urs ibn ‘Umayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Consult the women, so that the previously married woman may express her own view, and the permission of the virgin is her silence.”"],[1059,"Ibn ‘Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The previously married woman has more right concerning her affair, and the orphan girl is asked for permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence.”"],[1060,"Abu Umamah al-Bahili said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in the sermon of the Farewell Pilgrimage: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"],[1061,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the comfort of my eye has been placed in prayer.”"],[1062,"‘Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud said: the Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman should not closely examine another woman and then describe her to her husband as though he were looking at her.”"],[1063,"Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah will not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus.”"],[1064,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman must not be joined in marriage with her paternal aunt, nor with her maternal aunt.”"],[1065,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you made the private parts lawful.”"],[1066,"Muhammad ibn Hatib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What distinguishes the lawful from the unlawful is the beating of the drum and the raising of the voice in marriage.”"],[1067,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People are like a hundred camels; a man can hardly find a single riding camel among them.”"],[1068,"Ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should prevent his brother from making use of his wall for something from which he may benefit.”"],[1069,"Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will name your killer, then swear fifty oaths against him, and we will hand him over to you.”"],[1070,"Muʿawiyah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever drinks intoxicants, lash him. If he returns a fourth time, then kill him.”"],[1071,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perhaps a disheveled person, turned away from doors, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath.”"],[1072,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, killing a soul, and the false immersing oath.”"],[1073,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears falsely upon my pulpit, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[1074,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “No one should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal for more than three days.”"],[1075,"Salman ibn ʿAmir al-Dabbi said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “With the boy is a birth sacrifice, so shed blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him.”"],[1076,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I neither give you nor withhold from you by myself. I am only a distributor; I place it where I have been commanded.”"],[1077,"Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This affair will remain among Quraysh as long as two of them remain.”"],[1078,"Abu ʿAbs narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The feet of a servant do not become dusty in the path of Allah and then the Fire touch him.”"],[1079,"Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah supports this religion through people who have no share.”"],[1080,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no prize except in archery, camel-racing, or horse-racing.”"],[1081,"Ibn Masʿud narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.”"],[1082,"Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I do not give you nor withhold from you; I am only a distributor, placing where I have been commanded.”"],[1083,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is thrown from his mount in the path of Allah is a martyr.”"],[1084,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ibrahim the Prophet, peace be upon him, circumcised himself when he was eighty years old with an adze.”"],[1085,"Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, there is no true life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Anṣār and the Emigrants.”"],[1086,"ʿAlī reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me shall enter the Fire.”"],[1087,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever sees me has truly seen the truth, for Satan cannot take on my form.”"],[1088,"ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No person’s wealth has benefited us as much as the wealth of Abū Bakr.”"],[1089,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every prophet has a close disciple, and my close disciple is al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām.”"],[1090,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not revile Waraqah, for I have seen that he has one garden—or two gardens—in Paradise.”"],[1091,"Qurrah al-Muzanī (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The superiority of ʿĀ’ishah over other women is like the superiority of tharīd over all other foods.”"],[1092,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What an excellent people al-Azd are! Their speech is wholesome, their oaths are faithfully kept, and their hearts are pure.”"],[1093,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Harshness of heart and roughness are found in the East, while faith is among the people of the Ḥijāz.”"],[1094,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, place in Madinah twice the blessing that You placed in Makkah.”"],[1095,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “At the entrances of Madinah are angels. Neither the plague nor the Antichrist will enter it.”"],[1096,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘Glory and praise be to Allah, the Magnificent,’ a palm tree will be planted for him in Paradise.”"],[1097,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah says: ‘I am as My servant expects Me to be, and I am with him when he calls upon Me.’”"],[1098,"Mālik ibn Yasār al-Sukūnī, then al-ʿAwfī, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you ask Allah, ask Him with the palms of your hands, and do not ask Him with the backs of your hands.”"],[1099,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of the supplications of the oppressed, for they rise toward heaven like sparks.”"],[1100,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against the confederate armies and said: “O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Swift in reckoning, defeat the confederates. Defeat them and shake them severely.”"],[1101,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ would say between the two prostrations: “O Allah, forgive me, have mercy upon me, grant me well-being, guide me, and provide for me.”"],[1102,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought rain, he would say: “O Allah, give water to Your servants and Your animals, spread Your mercy, and revive Your dead land.”"],[1103,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If there is good in any of the treatments you use, it is in cupping.”"],[1104,"Usāmah ibn Sharīk narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “In black seed there is healing for every illness except death.”"],[1105,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Use antimony before sleeping, for it clears the eyesight and causes the eyelashes to grow.”"],[1106,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Use antimony, for it causes the eyelashes to grow, removes impurities from the eye, and clears the vision.”"],[1107,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no independent contagion, no hāmah, and no evil omen, but I love a good and hopeful word.”"],[1108,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A righteous dream is one of forty-six parts of prophethood.”"],[1109,"ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood.”"],[1110,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A truthful and righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood.”"],[1111,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the greatest lies is for a person to claim that his eyes saw what they did not see.” Another wording states: “Among the greatest lies are that a person attributes himself to someone other than his father, claims that his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see, or changes the boundary markers of land.”"],[1112,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever sees me has truly seen the truth, for Satan cannot assume my form.”"],[1113,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought that he would make him an heir.”"],[1114,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah loves to see the effect of His blessing upon His servant.”"],[1115,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A place in Paradise equal to the length of one of your whips is better than the world and everything within it.”"],[1116,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prayers heaviest upon the hypocrites are the ʿIshāʾ prayer and the Fajr prayer…” the remainder of the hadith."],[1117,"ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim narrated: I asked the Prophet ﷺ about game struck with a broad-headed arrow. He said: “Eat whatever it strikes with its sharp edge, but whatever it strikes with its broad side is an animal beaten to death.”"],[1118,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah destroy the Jews! Fat was forbidden to them, yet they sold it and consumed its price.”"],[1119,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer is to another believer like a building, each part strengthening the other.” He then interlaced his fingers."],[1120,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah have mercy upon Lot. He was indeed taking refuge in a strong support.”"],[1121,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Blessed is the one who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient, and who remains content.”"],[1122,"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Eat olive oil and apply it to your bodies, for it comes from a blessed tree.”"],[1123,"Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food most beloved to Allah is that over which many hands gather.”"],[1124,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There may be a disheveled person who is driven away from people’s doors, yet if he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would certainly fulfill it for him.”"],[1125,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays—Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī—narrated that when the Prophet ﷺ feared a people, he would say: “O Allah, we place You before them, and we seek refuge in You from their evil.”"],[1126,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesture with these two fingers—the middle finger and the index finger—and say: “I and the Hour have been sent like these two.”"],[1127,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer in relation to another believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other.” He then interlaced his fingers."],[1128,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘Glory and praise be to Allah, the Most Great,’ a palm tree will be planted for him in Paradise.”"],[1129,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesture with his fingers like this—with the middle finger and the one next to the thumb—and say: “I have been sent, and the Hour is like these two.”"],[1130,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not show mercy to him.”"],[1131,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is nothing heavier on the Scale than good character.”"],[1132,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty and faith have been joined together; when one of them is removed, the other is removed as well.”"],[1133,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Generous. He loves generosity and noble character, and He dislikes base and petty character.”"],[1134,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to our young and recognize the right of our elders is not of us.”"],[1135,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it, for it serves as discipline for them.”"],[1136,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer is one who is friendly and easy to befriend. There is no good in one who neither befriends others nor is easily befriended.”"],[1137,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yawning is from Satan. When one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can.”"],[1138,"Abū Shurayḥ al-Khuzāʿī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, I declare inviolable the rights of the two weak ones: the right of the orphan and the right of the woman.”"],[1139,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to our young and recognize the right of our elders is not of us.”"],[1140,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"],[1141,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"],[1142,"Nāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥārith narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the things that contribute to a person’s happiness are a righteous neighbor, a comfortable means of transportation, and a spacious home.”"],[1143,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a man to separate two people who are sitting together except with their permission.”"],[1144,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food most beloved to Allah is that over which the greatest number of hands gather.”"],[1145,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days. Whatever comes after that is charity.”"],[1146,"Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not keep close companionship except with a believer, and let none but a God-fearing person eat your food.”"],[1147,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved of your names to Allah are ʿAbdullāh and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.”"],[1148,"Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated: “My name was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Zaynab.” She said: Zaynab bint Jaḥsh also entered upon him, and her name had been Barrah, so he named her Zaynab."],[1149,"Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated: I saw Ibn ʿUmar speaking privately with a man. Another man came and inserted himself between them, so Ibn ʿUmar struck him on the chest and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When two people are speaking privately, a third person should not enter between them except with their permission.”"],[1150,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My soul has become foul.’ Rather, let him say, ‘My soul feels unsettled.’”"],[1151,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People are like one hundred camels; you can hardly find among them one suitable riding camel.”"],[1152,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should lie on his back and then place one leg over the other.”"],[1153,"Muʿādh ibn Anas, who was a Companion, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ride these animals while they are healthy, and leave them while they are healthy. Do not use them as chairs.”"],[1154,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A man was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ and cursed his camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O servant of Allah, do not travel with us on a cursed camel.”"],[1155,"Abū Zuhayr al-Numayrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill frogs, for their croaking is glorification of Allah, and do not kill bats; for when Bayt al-Maqdis was destroyed, the bat said: ‘My Lord, give me power over the sea so that I may drown them.’” In a shorter wording: “Do not kill frogs, for they are among the soldiers of Allah, the Exalted.”"],[1156,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: Misfortune and evil omens were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “If misfortune were to be in anything, it would be in the house, the woman, and the horse.”"],[1157,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a believer to boycott his brother for more than three days.”"],[1158,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever two people who insult one another say, the sin of it falls upon the one who began it, so long as the wronged person does not exceed the limit.”"],[1159,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the wrath of Allah, nor with the Fire.”"],[1160,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How many a disheveled person, driven away from people’s doors, is such that if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would surely fulfill his oath.”"],[1161,"The Mother of the Believers, ʿĀ’ishah, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a two-faced person to be honored or distinguished on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1162,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Wealth is not having an abundance of possessions. Rather, true wealth is the wealth of the soul.”"],[1163,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wealth is not having an abundance of possessions. True wealth is the wealth of the soul.”"],[1164,"Abū Qatādah and Abū al-Dahmāʾ narrated: We came across a man from the desert and asked him: “Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He replied: “Yes. I heard him say: ‘You will never leave something for the sake of Allah except that Allah will replace it for you with something better than it.’”"],[1165,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, there is no true life except the life of the Hereafter, so set right the Anṣār and the Muhājirūn.”"],[1166,"Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have not left behind me any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[1167,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The status and distinction that worldly people pursue is wealth.”"],[1168,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Glad tidings to the one who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient, and who is content.”"],[1169,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah loves to see the effect of His blessing upon His servant.”"],[1170,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look at the one who lets his izār hang low.”"],[1171,"Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best things with which to change this gray hair are henna and katam.”"],[1172,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"],[1173,"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"],[1174,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"],[1175,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Wearing silk and gold has been made lawful for the women of my Ummah and forbidden for its men.”"],[1176,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any woman who has applied incense perfume should not attend the later ʿIshāʾ prayer with us.”"],[1177,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you truly believes until his desires become subordinate to what I have brought.”"],[1178,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the greatest forms of jihād is a word of justice spoken in the presence of an unjust ruler.”"],[1179,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People are like a hundred camels among which you can scarcely find one suitable for riding.”"],[1180,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Hour will not be established until people build houses resembling decorated garments.”"],[1181,"Abū Burdah ibn Niyār narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The world will not pass away until it comes into the hands of a base son of a base man.”"],[1182,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand Jews of Isfahan will follow the Dajjāl, wearing ṭayālisah.”"],[1183,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “At the entrances of Madinah are angels. Neither the plague nor the Dajjāl will enter it.”"],[1184,"Abū Saʿīd and Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Near the end of time there will be a caliph who will distribute wealth without counting it.”"],[1185,"Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among your caliphs there will be a caliph who will scoop out wealth by the handful without counting it.”"],[1186,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first matters to be judged between the people on the Day of Resurrection will concern bloodshed.”"],[1187,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four rivers have been caused to flow from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile, Sayḥān, and Jayḥān.”"],[1188,"Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh?” He replied: “I saw people from my Ummah being driven toward Paradise in chains.”"],[1189,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The poor believers will enter Paradise five hundred years before their wealthy ones.”"],[1190,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The distance between the two shoulders of the disbeliever in the Fire will be a journey of three days for a swift rider.”"],[1191,"Muʿādh ibn Jabal may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever’s last words are, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ will enter Paradise.”"],[1192,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not deny your fathers, for whoever denies his father has committed an act of disbelief.”"],[1193,"Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them, reported: A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the major sins?” He replied: “Associating partners with Allah, despairing of relief from Allah, and losing hope in the mercy of Allah.”"],[1194,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ may Allah be pleased with them reported from the Prophet ﷺ: “Those who show mercy will be shown mercy by al-Raḥmān. Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One who is in the heaven will show mercy to you.”"],[1195,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is amazed at a young man who has no youthful inclination toward desire.”"],[1196,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah is more intensely joyful at the repentance of one of you than one of you is upon finding what he had lost.”"],[1197,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās may Allah be pleased with them reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw my Lord, Mighty and Majestic.” This is an abridged version of the preceding narration concerning the dream."],[1198,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah has angels who travel throughout the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my Ummah.”"],[1199,"Abū Hurayrah may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If a woman spends the night abandoning her husband’s bed, the angels curse her until she returns.”"],[1200,"Abū al-Dardāʾ may Allah be pleased with him reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “An undutiful child will not enter Paradise, nor one addicted to intoxicants, nor one who denies Divine Decree.”"],[1201,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Everything seeks forgiveness for the teacher of goodness, even the fish in the seas.”"],[1202,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah intends good for a servant, He grants him understanding of the religion and inspires him with right guidance.”"],[1203,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The virtue of knowledge is more beloved to me than the virtue of worship, and the best part of your religion is scrupulous piety.”"],[1204,"Abū al-Dardāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, the superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like the superiority of the moon over all the other heavenly bodies.”"],[1205,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge in Allah from knowledge that does not benefit.”"],[1206,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one should give public exhortation to the people except a ruler, one who has been authorized to do so, or a person seeking to show off and argue.”"],[1207,"Jundub ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite the Qurʾān as long as your hearts remain united concerning it. But when you begin to differ concerning it, then rise and leave it.”"],[1208,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever attributes to me what I did not say, let him take a seat in the Fire.”"],[1209,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever conceals knowledge, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[1210,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever narrates from me a report that he believes to be false is one of the liars.”"],[1211,"Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever narrates from me a report that he believes to be false is one of the liars.”"],[1212,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would cause hardship for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk with every wuḍūʾ.”"],[1213,"Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you sits to relieve himself, he should neither face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it.”"],[1214,"Abū Hurayrah , may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When a man sits between a woman’s four parts and then exerts himself with her, ghusl has become obligatory.”"],[1215,"ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from ghulūl.”"],[1216,"Buraydah ibn al-Husayb al-Aslami said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The covenant between us and them is the prayer; whoever abandons it has committed disbelief.”"],[1217,"Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Between a servant and disbelief and faith is the prayer; if he abandons it, then he has committed shirk.”"],[1218,"Sahl ibn Sa‘d al-Sa‘idi reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give glad tidings to those who walk in the darkness (to the prayer): they will have complete light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1219,"‘A’ishah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Jews have not envied you for anything as much as they have envied you for the greeting of peace and for saying ‘Amin.’”"],[1220,"Abu Mas‘ud al-Badri reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A person’s prayer is not sufficient until he straightens his back in bowing and prostration.” In another wording: “until a person straightens his spine in bowing and prostration.”"],[1221,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The closest a servant is to his Lord is while he is prostrating, so increase in supplication.”"],[1222,"Jubayr ibn Mut‘im said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have grown heavier, so do not get ahead of me in standing (transitions) in prayer, bowing, or prostration.”"],[1223,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you knew (or if they knew) what is in the front row, it would be decided by drawing lots.”"],[1224,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Congregational prayer is better than the prayer of one of you alone by twenty-five parts.” And in it: “The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the dawn prayer.” Then Abu Hurayrah would say: “Recite if you wish: ‘Indeed the recitation at dawn is witnessed.’” (17:78)"],[1225,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, but let them go out while they are not perfumed.”"],[1226,"Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should deliberately time his prayer to coincide with the rising of the sun or its setting.”"],[1227,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman, a donkey, and a dog cut off the prayer, and what protects against that is something like the rear of a saddle.”"],[1228,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should pray in a single garment with nothing of it on his shoulders.”"],[1229,"‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not raise your eyes to the sky lest they be tultama‘a (snatched away)”—meaning in prayer."],[1230,"Anas ibn Malik narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “If one of you becomes drowsy in prayer, then let him sleep until he knows what he is reciting.”"],[1231,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved places to Allah are their mosques, and the most detested places to Allah are their markets.”"],[1232,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best destinations to which riding mounts are taken are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House (the Kaʿbah).”"],[1233,"Anas was asked about garlic, and he said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever eats from this plant, let him not come near us, and let him not pray with us.”"],[1234,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever eats from this plant should not come near our mosques,” meaning garlic."],[1235,"Abū al-Jaʿd al-Ḍamrī (a Companion) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever leaves three Jumuʿahs out of negligence, Allah will stamp (seal) his heart.”"],[1236,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or a day after it.”"],[1237,"Samurah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever makes wuḍū’ on Friday, then that is fine and good; but whoever performs ghusl, then it is better.”"],[1238,"The Mother of the Believers, ʿĀ’ishah, reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “When the believer becomes ill, that purifies him just as the furnace purifies the impurity of iron.”"],[1239,"Anas ibn Mālik said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Allah said: If I test My servant in his two beloved things and he remains patient, I compensate him for them with Paradise.” Meaning: his two eyes."],[1240,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever is prompted at death to say: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ will enter Paradise.”"],[1241,"Muʿādh ibn Jabal reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever’s last words are ‘There is no god but Allah’ will enter Paradise.”"],[1242,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not from us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the calls of the pre-Islamic age.”"],[1243,"Samurah ibn Jundub reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Wear white garments, for they are purer and better, and shroud your dead in them.”"],[1244,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see a funeral, stand. And whoever follows it should not sit until it is set down.”"],[1245,"Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The deceased hears the sound of their sandals when they turn away from him,” meaning when they depart."],[1246,"‘Amr ibn Shu‘ayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, who said: “There is to be no driving of livestock in and no sending them from afar, and their charities are only to be taken in their own places.”"],[1247,"Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “In whatever is watered by rivers and rainclouds, tenths are due, and in whatever is watered by the water-drawing camel, half of one-tenth is due.”"],[1248,"Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The best charity is that which is given from surplus wealth, and begin with those whom you support.”"],[1249,"Umm Kulthum bint ʿUqbah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best charity is that given to a relative who harbors enmity.”"],[1250,"Abu Hurayrah said: Al-Hasan ibn ʿAli took a date from the dates of charity and put it in his mouth. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Spit it out, spit it out! Throw it away. Do you not know that we do not eat charity?”"],[1251,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were invited to a meal of a trotter, I would respond, and if a trotter were given to me as a gift, I would accept it.”"],[1252,"Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah frees people from the Fire at every breaking of the fast, and that is every night.”"],[1253,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fast upon seeing it, and break the fast upon seeing it. If the month is obscured from you, then count thirty.”"],[1254,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let not Bilal’s call to prayer prevent you from the pre-dawn meal, for there is some weakness in his sight.”"],[1255,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of a parent, the supplication of the fasting person, and the supplication of the traveler.”"],[1256,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you is invited to food while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting.”"],[1257,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six days of Shawwal, it is as though he fasted the whole year.”"],[1258,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, it is as though he fasted for a lifetime.”"],[1259,"Abu Qatadah al-Ansari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fasting three days of every month, and Ramadan to Ramadan, is like fasting for a lifetime.”"],[1260,"ʿAli ibn Abi Talib said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says: “These are not days for fasting; rather, they are days of eating, drinking, and remembrance.”"],[1261,"Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or a day after it.”"],[1262,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If he forgets and eats or drinks, then let him complete his fast, for it was only Allah who fed him and gave him drink.”"],[1263,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the call to prayer is made — meaning the dawn prayer — while one of you is in a state of major ritual impurity, then he should not fast that day.”"],[1264,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is overcome by vomiting does not have to make up the fast, but whoever vomits intentionally must make it up.”"],[1265,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Is it not the case that when she menstruates she neither prays nor fasts? That is part of the deficiency in her religion.”"],[1266,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “She remains for nights without praying, and she breaks the fast in Ramadan; this is the deficiency in religion.”"],[1267,"ʿA’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seek the Night of Decree in the odd nights of the last ten of Ramadan.”"],[1268,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “I looked at the moon on the morning after the Night of Decree, and I saw it as though it were half of a bowl.”"],[1269,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A woman must not travel for two days unless her husband or a mahram is with her.”"],[1270,"Al-Hajjaj ibn ʿAmr al-Ansari reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever suffers a broken limb or becomes lame may exit ihram, and he must perform pilgrimage the following year.”"],[1271,"Umm Jundub al-Azdiyyah narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ, when he departed, say: “O people, keep to calmness and dignity, and use pebbles like the pebbles used for slinging.”"],[1272,"Abdullah ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has angels who travel throughout the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[1273,"The Mother of the Believers Aishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man’s child is from his earnings, from the best of his earnings, so eat from their wealth.”"],[1274,"Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah have mercy on a man who is easygoing when he sells, when he buys, and when he asks for what is due to him.”"],[1275,"Ibn Umar and Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks his right should seek it with dignity, whether it is fully paid or not fully paid.”"],[1276,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the one who had a claim: “Take your right with dignity, whether fully or not fully.”"],[1277,"Abu al-Yusr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever gives respite to one in hardship, or remits part of what he owes, Allah will shade him in His shade.”"],[1278,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever bears arms against us is not from us, and whoever deceives us is not from us.”"],[1279,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The price of a dog, the fee of a fortune-teller, and the payment of a prostitute are not lawful.”"],[1280,"Abu Sa‘id said: Prices rose during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said, “If only you would set prices, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “I truly hope to leave you while none of you seeks from me redress for any injustice I committed against him.”"],[1281,"Sa‘id ibn Zayd ibn Nufayl said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever takes a handspan of land wrongfully will be encircled with it down to seven earths.”"],[1282,"The Mother of the Believers, Aishah, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever wrongfully takes even the measure of a handspan of land will be encircled with it from seven earths.”"],[1283,"Wa’il ibn Hujr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever usurps a man’s land unjustly will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”"],[1284,"Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Muslim women, no woman should consider insignificant a gift to her neighbor, even if it is only the hoof of a sheep.”"],[1285,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A child cannot fully repay his parent except if he finds him enslaved, buys him, and sets him free.”"],[1286,"‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do not follow one look with another, for the first is for you, but the second is not for you.”"],[1287,"ʿĀʾishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you are those who are best to their families, and I am the best of you to my family. When your companion dies, leave him alone.”"],[1288,"Talq ibn ‘Ali said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man calls his wife for his need, she should come to him, even if she is at the oven.”"],[1289,"Zayd ibn Arqam reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man calls his wife, she should respond, even if she is on the back of a saddle.”"],[1290,"‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said: We were on an expedition, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not come suddenly upon the women.” And he sent someone to announce to the people that they would be arriving the next morning."],[1291,"ʿA’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Part of a woman’s blessing is the ease of her proposal, the ease of her dowry, and the ease of her womb.”"],[1292,"ʿA’ishah narrated that she escorted a woman of the Ansar to her husband. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O ʿA’ishah, was there no amusement with you? For the Ansar are pleased by amusement.”"],[1293,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is an act of disbelief for a person to claim a lineage he does not know, or to deny it, even if slight.”"],[1294,"Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills a person under covenant without right, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him.”"],[1295,"A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whoever is afflicted by an injury in his body and then forgoes retaliation for the sake of Allah, it will be an expiation for him.”"],[1296,"Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blood-money for the fingers of the hands and feet is equal: ten camels for each finger.”"],[1297,"Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The injury caused by an animal is without liability, a well is without liability, a mine is without liability, and one-fifth is due on buried treasure.”"],[1298,"Abdullah ibn Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever you find committing the act of the people of Lut, then kill the one who does it and the one to whom it is done.”"],[1299,"Amr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pardon the prescribed punishments among yourselves, but whatever reaches me of a prescribed punishment has become obligatory.”"],[1300,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every boy is held in pledge by his birth sacrifice: it is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, his hair is shaved, and he is named.”"],[1301,"ʿAbd al-ʿAziz ibn Suhayb said: Anas was asked about garlic, so he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever eats from this plant must not come near us, nor pray with us.”"],[1302,"Abu Thaʿlabah al-Khushani said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."],[1303,"Ibn ʿAbbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My nation will drink wine near the end of time, calling it by a name other than its name.”"],[1304,"A woman narrated that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not make infusion from dates and raisins together. Make infusion from each one separately.”"],[1305,"Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave whose head is like a raisin is appointed over you.”"],[1306,"Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You must hear and obey in hardship and ease, in what you like and dislike, and even when others are favored over you.”"],[1307,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “An evening journey and a morning journey in the path of Allah are better than the world and all that is in it.”"],[1308,"Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever spends an expenditure in the path of Allah, it is written for him as seven hundred times its like.”"],[1309,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about migration, and he said: “There is no migration after the conquest, but there remains jihad and intention; and when you are called to go forth, then go forth.”"],[1310,"ʿUrwah al-Bariqi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils.”"],[1311,"ʿAbdullah ibn Abi Awfa said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against the Confederates and said: “O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Swift in reckoning, defeat the confederates. O Allah, defeat them and shake them.”"],[1312,"Anas ibn Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say on the day of Uhud: “O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth.”"],[1313,"Anas ibn Malik said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on an expedition, he would say: “O Allah, You are my support and my helper. By You I move, by You I charge, and by You I fight.”"],[1314,"ʿUrwah al-Bariqi said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils.”"],[1315,"ʿA’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about migration, and he said: “There is no migration after the Conquest, but there is jihad and intention. And when you are called to mobilize, then go forth.”"],[1316,"ʿAli ibn Abi Talib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of its women is Maryam bint ʿImran, and the best of its women is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid.”"],[1317,"ʿAbdullah ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not disfigure the face, for Allah created Adam upon the form of the Most Merciful.”"],[1318,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said on the Day of Badr, “This is Jibrīl, holding the head of his horse, wearing the equipment of war.”"],[1319,"Anas ibn Malik reported that on the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “O Allah! If You so will, You will not be worshipped upon the earth.”"],[1320,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against the Confederates, saying: “O Allah, Revealer of the Book and Swift in reckoning, defeat the Confederates. O Allah, defeat them and shake them.”"],[1321,"Khālid ibn al-Walīd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this nation is Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.”"],[1322,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.”"],[1323,"Anas ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī narrated: On the Day of Uḥud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: “O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth.”"],[1324,"Qays ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If faith were suspended at the Pleiades, men from among the sons of Persia would surely attain it.”"],[1325,"ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: When the Prophet ﷺ heard that ʿAlī had mentioned marrying the daughter of Abū Jahl, he said: “Fāṭimah is only a part of me. Whatever hurts her hurts me, and whatever causes her hardship causes me hardship.”"],[1326,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves the Anṣār, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Anṣār, Allah hates him.”"],[1327,"Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves the Anṣār loves them because of his love for me, and whoever hates the Anṣār hates them because of his hatred for me.”"],[1328,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you conquer Egypt, instruct one another to treat the Copts well, for they possess a covenant of protection and a bond of kinship.”"],[1329,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Faith will surely retreat to Madinah just as a snake retreats into its hole.”"],[1330,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of the West will continue to prevail upon the truth until the Hour is established.”"],[1331,"Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwāl, it will be as though he fasted for an entire lifetime.”"],[1332,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best remembrance is: ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ and the best supplication is: ‘All praise belongs to Allah.’”"],[1333,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has angels who travel throughout the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my nation.”"],[1334,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The servant is nearest to his Lord while he is prostrating, so supplicate abundantly.”"],[1335,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of a parent, the supplication of a fasting person, and the supplication of a traveler.”"],[1336,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on a military expedition, he would say: “O Allah, You are my support and my helper. Through You I maneuver, through You I charge, and through You I fight.”"],[1337,"Ṣuhayb narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encountered the enemy, he would say: “O Allah, through You I maneuver, through You I charge, and through You I fight.”"],[1338,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muḥammad as my Messenger,’ Paradise becomes obligatory for him.”"],[1339,"Abū Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever recites the final two verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah during the night, they will suffice him.”"],[1340,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge in Allah from knowledge that does not benefit.”"],[1341,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah created illness, He also created its cure, so seek treatment.”"],[1342,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are three things containing a cure for every illness except death: senna and sanūt.” Muḥammad ibn ʿUmārah, one of the narrators, said: “I forgot the third.”"],[1343,"Jundub ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Recite the Qur’an as long as your hearts remain united upon it. When you begin to differ, rise and leave it.”"],[1344,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Abū Mūsā, you have certainly been given a flute-like voice from among the melodious voices of the family of David.”"],[1345,"Abū Masʿūd al-Badrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever recites the final two verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah during the night, they will suffice him.”"],[1346,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Begin fasting when you see the crescent, and end the fast when you see it. If the month is obscured from you, then count thirty days.”"],[1347,"Al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The heart of the son of Adam changes more rapidly than a cooking pot when it reaches a full boil.”"],[1348,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is a tree in Paradise beneath whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years.”"],[1349,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever plays backgammon is as though he dipped his hand into the flesh and blood of a pig.”"],[1350,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said on the day of Badr: “This is Gabriel holding the head of his horse, wearing the equipment of war.”"],[1351,"ʿUrwah al-Bāriqī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Goodness remains tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils.”"],[1352,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Successful indeed is the one who embraces Islam, is provided with what is sufficient, and is made content by Allah with what He has given him.”"],[1353,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I am only a human being like you. I forget just as you forget, so when I forget, remind me.”"],[1354,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against the confederate armies, saying: “O Allah, Revealer of the Book and Swift in reckoning, defeat the confederates. O Allah, defeat them and shake them.”"],[1355,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Successful indeed is the one who accepts Islam, is provided with enough to meet his needs, and whom Allah makes content with what He has given him.”"],[1356,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has left no excuse for a person whose lifespan He prolonged until he reached sixty years of age.”"],[1357,"ʿĀ’ishah, Mother of the Believers, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seek the Night of Decree during the odd-numbered nights of the last ten nights of Ramadan.”"],[1358,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The disbeliever eats with seven intestines, while the believer eats with one intestine.”"],[1359,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Muslim eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”"],[1360,"Jābir and Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”"],[1361,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”"],[1362,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who truly maintains family ties is not merely the one who reciprocates kindness. Rather, the true maintainer of family ties is the one who continues to maintain them even when his relatives cut him off.”"],[1363,"Ibn ʿAbbās said regarding the words: “Those who avoid the major sins and immoralities except for minor slips”: “If You forgive, O Allah, You forgive sins in abundance; and which of Your servants has not committed some minor slip?”"],[1364,"Jābir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The ten are the ten days of al-Aḍḥā, the odd is the Day of ʿArafah, and the even is the Day of Sacrifice.”"],[1365,"Umm Kulthūm bint ʿUqbah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best charity is that given to a relative who harbors hostility toward you.”"],[1366,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb—or a man from the Anṣār—narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever recites ‘Say: He is Allah, One,’ it is as though he has recited one-third of the Qur’an.”"],[1367,"Saʿīd ibn Yazīd al-Azdī narrated that a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He said: “I advise you to be modest before Allah just as you would be modest before a righteous man from among your people.”"],[1368,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is granted a favor and mentions it has shown gratitude for it, while whoever conceals it has shown ingratitude for it.”"],[1369,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ: “Those who show mercy will be shown mercy by the Most Merciful. Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One above the heavens will show mercy to you.”"],[1370,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, among the gravest forms of usury is unjustly attacking the honor of a Muslim.”"],[1371,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No servant loves another servant for the sake of Allah except that he thereby honors his Lord, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[1372,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ used to instruct people to treat enslaved persons well, saying: “Feed them from what you eat, clothe them from what you wear, and do not torture the creation of Allah.”"],[1373,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An enslaved person is entitled to his food and clothing, and he must not be burdened with work beyond what he is capable of.”"],[1374,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a slave is sincere to his master and worships Allah well, he receives his reward twice.”"],[1375,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a slave fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he receives two rewards.”"],[1376,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who truly maintains kinship is not merely the one who reciprocates. Rather, the true maintainer of kinship is the one who, when his relatives sever ties with him, continues to maintain ties with them.”"],[1377,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The bond of kinship is a branch connected to al-Raḥmān. Whoever severs it, Allah forbids Paradise to him.”"],[1378,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer in relation to another believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other.” Al-Bukhārī added: He then interlaced his fingers."],[1379,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us, and whoever deceives us is not of us.”"],[1380,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, among the gravest forms of usury is unjustly attacking the honor of a Muslim.”"],[1381,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the believer wears down and overcomes his devils just as one of you wears down his camel during a journey.”"],[1382,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Muslim women, no female neighbor should belittle what she gives to another female neighbor, even if it is only a sheep’s hoof.”"],[1383,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Your permission to enter upon me is that the curtain be raised and that you hear my private conversation, until I tell you otherwise.”"],[1384,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you visits his brother and sits with him, he should not get up to leave until he seeks his permission.”"],[1385,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not greet with the greeting of the Jews and Christians, for their greeting is by means of the hands, the head, and gestures.”"],[1386,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rider should give salām to the one who is walking, the one who is walking to the one who is sitting, and the smaller group to the larger group.”"],[1387,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The younger should give salām to the older, the one passing by to the one sitting, and the smaller group to the larger group.”"],[1388,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mounted person should give salām to the one walking, the one walking to the one standing, and the smaller group to the larger group.”"],[1389,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Muslim eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”"],[1390,"Jābir and Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”"],[1391,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”"],[1392,"Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The disbeliever eats with seven intestines, while the believer eats with one intestine.”"],[1393,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If the one who drinks while standing knew what was in his stomach, he would make himself vomit.”"],[1394,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days. Whatever exceeds that is charity, and every good deed is charity.”"],[1395,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If I were invited to a meal consisting only of a sheep’s lower leg, I would accept the invitation; and if a sheep’s lower leg were given to me as a gift, I would accept it.”"],[1396,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The invitations of two people competing with each other in ostentation are not to be accepted, nor is their food to be eaten.”"],[1397,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever attributes his allegiance to patrons other than his true patrons has removed the bond of faith from his neck.”"],[1398,"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no part of the body except that it complains of the tongue because of the sharpness of its speech.”"],[1399,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of my Ummah is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.”"],[1400,"ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of my Ummah is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.”"],[1401,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever plays nardashīr, it is as though he has dipped his hand into the flesh and blood of a pig.”"],[1402,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you were forgiven for what you do to animals, much would indeed be forgiven for you.”"],[1403,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and do not compete against one another in rivalry. Be servants of Allah as brothers.”"],[1404,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is not one who curses others, attacks people’s honor, speaks obscenely, or uses foul language.”"],[1405,"Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs deeds so that people will hear of them, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.”"],[1406,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks reputation through his deeds, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.”"],[1407,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks reputation through his deeds, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.”"],[1408,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The strong man is not the one who defeats others in wrestling. The truly strong man is the one who controls himself when angry.”"],[1409,"ʿAbbād ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated: My father and I went out seeking knowledge among this clan of the Anṣār before they passed away. The first person we met was Abū al-Yasar, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. With him was a servant boy carrying a bundle of written sheets. Abū al-Yasar was wearing a cloak and a Maʿāfirī garment, and his servant was likewise wearing a cloak and a Maʿāfirī garment. My father said to him: “Uncle, I can see signs of anger on your face.” He replied: “Indeed. So-and-so, son of so-and-so from Banū Ḥarām, owed me some money. I went to his family, greeted them, and asked, ‘Is he here?’ They replied, ‘No.’ Then a young son of his who was nearing puberty came out to me. I asked him, ‘Where is your father?’ He replied, ‘He heard your voice and went into my mother’s enclosed room.’ So I called out, ‘Come out to me, for I know where you are.’ He came out, and I asked, ‘What made you hide from me?’ He said, ‘By Allah, I will tell you the truth and not lie to you. By Allah, I feared that I might speak to you and lie, or make you a promise and then break it. You were a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and by Allah, I am in financial hardship.’ I said, ‘By Allah?’ He said, ‘By Allah.’ I asked again, ‘By Allah?’ He replied, ‘By Allah.’ I asked a third time, ‘By Allah?’ He replied, ‘By Allah.’” Abū al-Yasar then brought the written document of the debt and erased it with his own hand. He said: “If you later become able to repay, then repay me. Otherwise, you are released from it. I testify by these two eyes of mine”—and he placed his fingers upon his eyes—“and these two ears of mine, and this heart of mine that retained it”—and he pointed to his heart—“that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever gives respite to a debtor in hardship, or remits his debt, Allah will shade him in His shade.’” I said to him: “Uncle, why do you not take your servant’s cloak and give him your Maʿāfirī garment, then take his Maʿāfirī garment and give him your cloak, so that each of you would have a matching set of garments?” He wiped my head and said: “O Allah, bless him.” Then he said: “My nephew, these two eyes of mine saw, these two ears of mine heard, and this heart of mine retained”—and he pointed to his heart—“the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: ‘Feed them from what you yourselves eat, and clothe them from what you yourselves wear.’” He continued: “Giving him some of the possessions of this world is easier for me than having him take from my good deeds on the Day of Resurrection.” Then we continued until we came to Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh in his mosque. He was praying wrapped in a single garment. I stepped past the people and sat between him and the qiblah. I said: “May Allah have mercy on you. Are you praying in a single garment while your outer cloak is lying beside you?” He placed his hand upon my chest like this, spreading and bending his fingers, and said: “I wanted a foolish person like you to come in, see how I do it, and then do the same.” Jābir continued: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in this very mosque carrying a date-palm stalk from Ibn Ṭāb. He saw some phlegm on the qiblah wall of the mosque and scraped it away with the stalk. Then he turned toward us and said: “Which of you would like Allah to turn away from him?” We became subdued and silent. He repeated: “Which of you would like Allah to turn away from him?” We remained subdued. He asked a third time: “Which of you would like Allah to turn away from him?” We said: “None of us, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “When one of you stands to pray, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is before his face. So let him not spit in front of himself or to his right. Let him spit to his left beneath his left foot. If something suddenly overcomes him, then let him do this with his garment.” He then folded part of his garment over another part. Then he said: “Bring me some perfume.” A young man from the neighborhood hurried to his family and returned with some khalūq perfume in his palm. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it, placed it on the tip of the palm stalk, and smeared it over the place where the phlegm had been. Jābir said: “From that incident came your practice of placing perfume in your mosques.” We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Baṭn Buwāṭ, while he was seeking al-Majdī ibn ʿAmr al-Juhanī. Five, six, or seven of us would take turns riding a single camel used for carrying water. When the turn of a man from the Anṣār came to ride his camel, he made it kneel, mounted it, and urged it forward. The camel hesitated somewhat, so the man said: “Move! May Allah curse you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who is this person cursing his camel?” The man replied: “It is me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Get down from it. Do not accompany us with an animal that has been cursed. Do not supplicate against yourselves, do not supplicate against your children, and do not supplicate against your wealth, lest you happen to coincide with a time in which Allah is asked for something and He answers you.” We continued traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until late afternoon, when we approached a watering place belonging to some Arabs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who will go ahead of us, plaster the watering trough, drink, and prepare water for us?” Jābir said: I stood and said: “Here is a man, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who will go with Jābir?” Jabbār ibn Ṣakhr stood up. We went to the well, drew one or two buckets of water into the trough, then plastered and repaired it. We continued drawing water until we filled it completely. The first person to arrive was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He asked: “Do you give permission?” We replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He lowered his she-camel’s head into the water and she drank. He then pulled up her reins; she spread her legs and urinated. He moved her aside and made her kneel. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the trough and performed wuḍūʾ from it. I stood and performed wuḍūʾ from the remaining water from the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Jabbār ibn Ṣakhr went away to relieve himself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray. I was wearing a cloak and tried to cross its two ends over my shoulders, but it was too short. It had loose hanging ends, so I turned it around, crossed its two ends, and bent my neck down to hold it in place. Then I came and stood on the left side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He took me by the hand, moved me around, and placed me on his right. Then Jabbār ibn Ṣakhr returned, performed wuḍūʾ, and stood on the left side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took both of us by the hands and moved us backward until he placed us behind him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept glancing toward me, though at first I did not notice. Then I became aware of him. He gestured with his hand, meaning: “Tighten it around your waist.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: “O Jābir.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “If the garment is wide, cross its two ends over your shoulders. If it is narrow, fasten it around your waist.” We continued traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The daily provision of each one of us was a single date. A man would suck on it and then wrap it up in his garment. We would also strike the trees with our bows so that their leaves fell, and we would eat them, until the sides of our mouths became ulcerated. One day, by Allah, one of our men was mistakenly not given his date. We carried him along, supporting him because of his weakness, and testified that he had not received it. So he was given his date, whereupon he stood up and took it. We continued traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached a broad valley. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went away to relieve himself, and I followed him carrying a small vessel of water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked around but saw nothing behind which he could conceal himself. There were two trees on the edge of the valley. He went to one of them, took hold of one of its branches, and said: “Come with me by the permission of Allah.” It moved along with him like a camel with a nose-peg that submits to its handler. He then came to the other tree, took one of its branches, and said: “Come with me by the permission of Allah.” It moved along with him in the same way. When he reached the midpoint between the two trees, he brought them together and said: “Join together over me by the permission of Allah.” And the two trees joined together. Jābir said: I hurried away because I feared that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might become aware of how close I was and move even farther away. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād’s wording has: “move farther away.” I sat speaking to myself. Then I happened to glance over and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approaching. The two trees had separated again, each standing upon its own trunk. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stop briefly and move his head like this—Abū Ismāʿīl gestured with his head to the right and left—then he continued toward me. When he reached me, he said: “O Jābir, did you see where I was standing?” I replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Go to the two trees and cut a branch from each one. Bring them back, and when you reach the place where I stood, place one branch on your right and one branch on your left.” Jābir said: I stood up, took a stone, broke it and sharpened it until it had a cutting edge. I went to the two trees, cut a branch from each, and dragged them back until I reached the place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had stood. I placed one branch on my right and the other on my left. Then I caught up with him and said: “I have done it, O Messenger of Allah. Why did you ask me to do that?” He replied: “I passed by two graves whose occupants are being punished, and I wished, through my intercession, that their punishment might be lightened for as long as the two branches remain fresh.” We returned to the camp. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Jābir, call out for water for ablution.” I called: “Is there any water for ablution? Any water for ablution? Any water for ablution?” Then I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I could not find a single drop among the travelers.” There was a man from the Anṣār who used to cool water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in worn waterskins hung upon a wooden frame. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Go to so-and-so, son of so-and-so, the Anṣārī, and see whether there is anything in his waterskins.” I went and checked them. I found only a single drop remaining at the mouth of one worn waterskin—so little that if I poured it out, the dry skin itself would absorb it. I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I found only one drop at the mouth of one waterskin. If I poured it out, the dry waterskin itself would absorb it.” He said: “Go and bring it to me.” I brought it to him. He took it in his hand, began saying something that I could not understand, and squeezed it with his hands. Then he gave it back to me and said: “O Jābir, call for a large basin.” I called out: “Bring the travelers’ basin!” It was brought, carried by several people, and I placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spread his hand in the basin, separated his fingers, and placed his hand at the bottom of it. Then he said: “Take it, O Jābir. Pour over my hand and say: ‘In the name of Allah.’” I poured and said: “In the name of Allah.” Then I saw water bursting forth from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The basin began filling and swirling with water until it became full. He said: “O Jābir, call everyone who needs water.” The people came and drew water until they were completely satisfied. I asked: “Is there anyone left who still needs water?” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted his hand from the basin while it was still full. The people complained of hunger to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Perhaps Allah will feed you.” We came to the seashore. The sea surged strongly and cast out a huge sea creature. We lit a fire beside it, cooked and roasted from it, and ate until we were full. Jābir said: Five of us, including myself and several others whom he named, entered into the socket of its eye without anyone outside being able to see us. Then we came out and took one of its ribs and stood it upright like an arch. We called for the tallest man among the travelers, the largest camel among them, and the largest riding cushion among them. The rider passed beneath that rib without even needing to lower his head."],[1410,"ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī narrated: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Should I leave my camel untied and rely upon Allah?” He replied: “Tie it, and rely upon Allah.”"],[1411,"Abū Bakrah narrated: A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, which people are best?” He replied: “The one whose life is long and whose deeds are good.” The man asked: “And which people are worst?” He replied: “The one whose life is long and whose deeds are evil.”"],[1412,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the dinar and the dirham destroyed those who came before you, and they will be a cause of your destruction as well.”"],[1413,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Successful indeed is the one who accepts Islam, is provided with what is sufficient for him, and whom Allah makes content with what He has given him.”"],[1414,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at the one who drags his garment out of arrogance.”"],[1415,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Five things are from the fiṭrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and plucking the armpit hair.”"],[1416,"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1417,"Abū Qatādah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If it concerns your worldly affairs, then that is for you; but if it concerns your religion, then refer it to me.”"],[1418,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of the West will continue to remain manifest upon the truth until the Hour is established.”"],[1419,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever introduces into this matter of ours something that does not belong to it, it is rejected.”"],[1420,"Al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad said: I do not feel secure regarding anyone after what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The heart of the son of Ādam changes more rapidly than a cooking pot when it has reached a full boil.”"],[1421,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever separates himself from the community by even a handspan has removed the bond of Islam from his neck.”"],[1422,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Hour will not be established until there occur within my Ummah incidents of the earth swallowing people, transformation, and stones being cast down upon them.”"],[1423,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not be established until no one on earth says: ‘Allah, Allah.’”"],[1424,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The signs are like beads strung together on a thread. When the thread breaks, they follow one another.”"],[1425,"Al-Nawwās ibn Samʿān narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Muslims will use the bows, arrows, and shields of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj as fuel for seven years.”"],[1426,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The first of the signs of the Hour will be a fire that gathers the people from the East to the West.”"],[1427,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree beneath whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years.”"],[1428,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Paradise is closer to each one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise.”"]]);
